WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

2
00:03:02.750 --> 00:03:04.000
You saved her life.

3
00:03:05.083 --> 00:03:06.458
Give me a blanket!

4
00:03:13.458 --> 00:03:15.208
I told you not to go!

5
00:03:15.292 --> 00:03:16.583
You'll stay in the hold!

6
00:03:16.667 --> 00:03:18.583
I don't wanna see you
until we reach Marseille.

7
00:03:19.583 --> 00:03:20.583
What's wrong?

8
00:03:21.625 --> 00:03:26.167
You think I'm harsh?
I know I am. I take pride in that.

9
00:03:26.875 --> 00:03:27.875
Go!

10
00:03:31.667 --> 00:03:33.583
Come on. everyone to your stations!

11
00:03:36.083 --> 00:03:38.667
Put her somewhere dry
before she freezes to death.

12
00:03:38.750 --> 00:03:39.750
Wait!

13
00:03:42.958 --> 00:03:43.958
Go!

14
00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:23.000
Sleep well?

15
00:04:24.125 --> 00:04:25.958
You have something that belongs to me.

16
00:04:27.917 --> 00:04:30.167
I've never seen
the Emperor's handwriting before.

17
00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:32.833
Give me back that letter.

18
00:04:34.375 --> 00:04:35.500
I don't think so.

19
00:04:37.542 --> 00:04:38.583
What do you want?

20
00:04:39.583 --> 00:04:41.333
A good reason not to turn you in.

21
00:04:44.042 --> 00:04:45.208
Try money.

22
00:04:46.083 --> 00:04:47.458
It usually works.

23
00:04:47.542 --> 00:04:48.583
I don't have any.

24
00:04:50.292 --> 00:04:51.292
But I have friends.

25
00:04:53.542 --> 00:04:55.792
If you say anything
about this letter to anyone.

26
00:04:56.333 --> 00:04:59.333
they will find you and they will kill you.

27
00:05:00.125 --> 00:05:01.542
Captain Danglars.

28
00:05:38.542 --> 00:05:39.542
Sir?

29
00:05:41.375 --> 00:05:43.208
I've caused you a lot of trouble.

30
00:05:44.250 --> 00:05:45.875
I don't know how to thank you.

31
00:05:47.542 --> 00:05:48.833
You just did.

32
00:05:51.083 --> 00:05:52.083
Take care.

33
00:05:54.083 --> 00:05:55.083
Miss...

34
00:05:57.208 --> 00:05:58.208
Angéle.

35
00:05:59.458 --> 00:06:00.458
Edmond.

36
00:06:01.917 --> 00:06:03.583
I'll never forget your courage.

37
00:06:05.333 --> 00:06:06.667
but you must forget my name.

38
00:06:09.375 --> 00:06:10.458
Goodbye. Edmond.

39
00:06:11.667 --> 00:06:12.958
Goodbye. Angéle.

40
00:06:24.375 --> 00:06:25.625
Morrel wants to see you.

41
00:06:32.250 --> 00:06:34.917
We had changed the watch.
We were off Cap Corse.

42
00:06:35.417 --> 00:06:38.208
The swells were strong.
We were 200 fathoms from the wreck.

43
00:06:38.292 --> 00:06:39.625
Give me the Captain's log.

44
00:06:40.625 --> 00:06:42.542
We started kicking around the debris

45
00:06:42.625 --> 00:06:44.792
when Dantés tried
to take the longboat out.

46
00:06:44.875 --> 00:06:47.250
I told him not to.
It was a foolish thing to do.

47
00:06:47.625 --> 00:06:48.708
Is that true?

48
00:06:48.792 --> 00:06:52.542
Yes. sir. Except it wasn't foolish.
we'd do it for any of our crew.

49
00:06:52.625 --> 00:06:54.917
- It was my decision! I ordered...
- I took charge--

50
00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:56.917
...to turn the ship around. and he dove in.

51
00:06:58.458 --> 00:06:59.583
You dove.

52
00:06:59.667 --> 00:07:02.000
Captain Danglars
didn't say I couldn't dive.

53
00:07:02.375 --> 00:07:03.375
That's enough!

54
00:07:04.292 --> 00:07:05.542
Did you see that insolence?

55
00:07:07.333 --> 00:07:10.667
Mr. Morrel. I'm telling you.
this boy is out of control.

56
00:07:12.167 --> 00:07:13.625
I don't want to sail with him.

57
00:07:16.792 --> 00:07:18.583
You won't sail with him anymore.

58
00:07:18.667 --> 00:07:20.000
See. I warned you.

59
00:07:20.625 --> 00:07:22.833
Because you'll never sail for me again.

60
00:07:23.917 --> 00:07:24.917
Excuse me?

61
00:07:26.375 --> 00:07:28.542
How could you let a woman drown?

62
00:07:30.083 --> 00:07:31.833
I saved your shipment. Mr. Morrel.

63
00:07:31.917 --> 00:07:34.042
And Dantés saved my honor. Danglars.

64
00:07:34.125 --> 00:07:36.458
- Captain Danglars.
- You're no longer captain.

65
00:07:37.917 --> 00:07:39.542
Go and pack your things.

66
00:07:40.125 --> 00:07:41.917
I'll have your pay settled.

67
00:07:42.542 --> 00:07:44.417
We don't even know who that woman is.

68
00:07:44.500 --> 00:07:47.583
I know what you did.
and that's all I need to know.

69
00:08:02.417 --> 00:08:04.083
Hey. little guy. come here!

70
00:08:06.875 --> 00:08:08.042
Come!

71
00:08:09.458 --> 00:08:12.125
Now. let that be a lesson to you. okay?

72
00:08:13.167 --> 00:08:17.917
When you're a man. you don't hide
behind your rank or under a table.

73
00:08:20.708 --> 00:08:24.208
Edmond. this is my grandson. Maximilian.

74
00:08:25.083 --> 00:08:26.667
Nice to meet you. Maximilian.

75
00:08:26.750 --> 00:08:30.667
Maximilian. this is Captain Dantés.

76
00:08:30.750 --> 00:08:32.917
- Hello. Captain.
- So. how old--

77
00:08:35.083 --> 00:08:36.333
Captain?

78
00:08:36.417 --> 00:08:39.208
Yes. Try to prove yourself worthy. Edmond.

79
00:08:41.083 --> 00:08:43.958
Of course. sir. Of course.

80
00:09:08.375 --> 00:09:09.500
Good boy.

81
00:09:16.917 --> 00:09:18.042
Edmond!

82
00:09:23.167 --> 00:09:25.958
- I can't believe you're here!
- I...

83
00:09:26.625 --> 00:09:28.792
- I have to tell you something.
- That you love me.

84
00:09:29.292 --> 00:09:32.458
- Yes. of course. but--
- No buts.

85
00:09:32.542 --> 00:09:35.125
- Wait. but--
- You're doing it again!

86
00:09:42.375 --> 00:09:44.583
You're kissing a future captain.

87
00:09:47.333 --> 00:09:48.583
- You?
- Yes.

88
00:09:51.917 --> 00:09:55.167
- That means we can--
- Yes. we can.

89
00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:08.167
I missed you.

90
00:10:10.042 --> 00:10:11.750
I missed you so much.

91
00:10:35.458 --> 00:10:36.542
See you later.

92
00:11:02.958 --> 00:11:05.958
- Edmond! Edmond.
- Juliette.

93
00:11:06.042 --> 00:11:07.500
- How are you?
- And you?

94
00:11:07.583 --> 00:11:09.625
Yes. I'm fine.

95
00:11:10.417 --> 00:11:11.625
It's Edmond. Louis' son!

96
00:11:11.708 --> 00:11:13.292
- Good morning. sir.
- Good morning.

97
00:11:14.250 --> 00:11:16.083
Where's my father? I have to see him.

98
00:11:16.167 --> 00:11:18.417
- At home.
- See you later.

99
00:11:29.208 --> 00:11:31.875
Smile a little. It's good news.

100
00:11:32.875 --> 00:11:34.208
You look sad.

101
00:11:35.083 --> 00:11:36.125
It's joy.

102
00:11:38.708 --> 00:11:40.042
I'm so proud of you!

103
00:11:42.833 --> 00:11:43.833
Captain!

104
00:11:44.500 --> 00:11:45.500
Captain.

105
00:11:47.083 --> 00:11:49.583
Did you tell Mr. and Mrs. de Morcerf?

106
00:11:49.667 --> 00:11:52.417
No. not yet. I wanted to tell you first.

107
00:11:54.750 --> 00:11:56.083
Everything will change. Dad.

108
00:11:56.875 --> 00:11:58.167
We have to tell them.

109
00:11:59.500 --> 00:12:00.917
This is thanks to them.

110
00:12:02.042 --> 00:12:03.125
And to you too.

111
00:12:03.917 --> 00:12:06.125
I didn't pay for you to go to Navy School.

112
00:12:08.958 --> 00:12:10.333
Go on. Son.

113
00:12:11.333 --> 00:12:12.708
go pay your respects.

114
00:12:27.625 --> 00:12:28.750
How about a toast?

115
00:12:29.500 --> 00:12:32.375
I raise my glass
to the memory of your mother. Edmond.

116
00:12:32.458 --> 00:12:33.875
First. because we miss her

117
00:12:34.792 --> 00:12:38.042
and because she gave birth
to Marseille's youngest captain!

118
00:12:38.125 --> 00:12:39.208
- Bravo!
- Yes. go ahead.

119
00:12:39.292 --> 00:12:41.292
Clap. it will make him uncomfortable.

120
00:12:44.000 --> 00:12:45.458
That's it. Perfect.

121
00:12:45.542 --> 00:12:49.542
But most of all. because Mathilde Dantés

122
00:12:49.625 --> 00:12:55.417
looked after a future French nobleman
with a heroic destiny.

123
00:12:55.500 --> 00:12:57.917
One of Europe's most handsome officers.

124
00:12:58.000 --> 00:13:01.542
I'm speaking of Fernand de Morcerf.
at your service.

125
00:13:03.958 --> 00:13:04.958
Louis!

126
00:13:05.042 --> 00:13:06.417
Come and toast to the occasion.

127
00:13:06.500 --> 00:13:10.250
Thank you. sir. Maybe later.

128
00:13:11.875 --> 00:13:15.833
Please. scold Mercedes for me.
She doesn't listen to me anymore.

129
00:13:15.917 --> 00:13:18.250
You'll see.
she'll be late for her own wedding.

130
00:13:18.333 --> 00:13:19.542
Oh! Finally!

131
00:13:20.083 --> 00:13:23.583
I'm sorry I'm late. Auntie!
Oh! Hello. Uncle.

132
00:13:23.667 --> 00:13:27.417
Horace had a mind of his own.
I was this close to giving him a spanking.

133
00:13:27.500 --> 00:13:29.292
- Mercédés!
- Mr. Count.

134
00:13:29.375 --> 00:13:31.625
- Who is this gentleman?
- No. it's a horse. Mom.

135
00:13:31.708 --> 00:13:33.250
But he's from a good family.

136
00:13:33.333 --> 00:13:35.583
- Hello. Cousin.
- Hello. Cousin.

137
00:13:38.208 --> 00:13:40.667
- Edmond.
- Mercédés.

138
00:13:40.750 --> 00:13:44.708
I hope you're ready to party.
our Edmond has some great news for you.

139
00:13:45.833 --> 00:13:46.833
Yes.

140
00:13:49.875 --> 00:13:52.583
Yes. I'm going to be a captain.

141
00:13:52.667 --> 00:13:54.625
Captain of the Pharaoh. It's official.

142
00:13:56.333 --> 00:13:57.333
Really?

143
00:13:58.333 --> 00:14:00.333
- Congratulations.
- To the captain!

144
00:14:19.958 --> 00:14:20.958
Got it.

145
00:14:22.583 --> 00:14:26.042
To your health!
I'm really happy for you. my friend.

146
00:14:26.125 --> 00:14:28.542
Yes. I'm really happy
for me too. my friend.

147
00:14:28.625 --> 00:14:30.833
- Cheers!
- You're getting a new uniform?

148
00:14:31.583 --> 00:14:33.125
And more importantly. a new paycheck.

149
00:14:33.708 --> 00:14:36.375
He'll finally be able to enjoy life.
have a good time.

150
00:14:36.458 --> 00:14:38.000
And we'll show him how it's done.

151
00:14:38.542 --> 00:14:40.083
And I'll be able to get married.

152
00:14:42.917 --> 00:14:45.792
- What's this about?
- You're going to be my witness.

153
00:14:45.875 --> 00:14:47.708
- Don't count on it.
- Yes.

154
00:14:47.792 --> 00:14:51.417
Witness to a disaster!
M-- Mercédés. say something!

155
00:14:51.917 --> 00:14:53.625
Well. I tried. But what can I do?

156
00:14:53.708 --> 00:14:55.917
- He's madly in love.
- Completely mad.

157
00:14:56.000 --> 00:14:59.083
- Mad. mad.
- Does she know?

158
00:14:59.167 --> 00:15:00.750
I mean. is she okay with it?

159
00:15:00.833 --> 00:15:03.500
- Yeah. from what she told me.
- I know!

160
00:15:05.417 --> 00:15:07.167
- It's Juliette.
- Who?

161
00:15:07.250 --> 00:15:09.500
- No!
- The laundry girl with the naughty eyes.

162
00:15:09.583 --> 00:15:12.250
No. it's not Juliette!

163
00:15:13.250 --> 00:15:16.000
No. she's... a real woman.

164
00:15:17.000 --> 00:15:18.000
Very beautiful.

165
00:15:18.583 --> 00:15:19.833
Not just beautiful.

166
00:15:21.958 --> 00:15:25.875
- Mysterious and beguiling.
- Yes! Yes. that too.

167
00:15:25.958 --> 00:15:26.958
Who is she?

168
00:15:31.833 --> 00:15:33.042
It's your cousin.

169
00:15:34.750 --> 00:15:36.875
Mercédés Herrera de Morcerf.

170
00:15:38.333 --> 00:15:39.333
You?

171
00:15:39.500 --> 00:15:41.667
- Yes!
- We're getting married. Fernand.

172
00:15:41.750 --> 00:15:43.458
Are you out of your mind?

173
00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:45.583
Your mother will never allow it.

174
00:15:45.667 --> 00:15:48.167
Do you really think
my mother can say "no" to me?

175
00:15:49.208 --> 00:15:52.542
Besides. you'll help to convince her.
You were always her favorite nephew.

176
00:17:38.583 --> 00:17:39.708
Amen.

177
00:17:45.917 --> 00:17:49.917
I bring. signed by Mr. de Villefort.
the King's Prosecutor.

178
00:17:50.000 --> 00:17:53.042
a warrant for the arrest of Edmond Dantés.

179
00:17:56.042 --> 00:17:58.083
- Come with us. sir.
- What's going on?

180
00:17:58.167 --> 00:18:00.667
- No. There's got to be an explanation.
- Leave him alone.

181
00:18:00.750 --> 00:18:02.250
- Come on!
- Let go of me.

182
00:18:03.000 --> 00:18:04.958
- Wait.
- Fernand. do something.

183
00:18:05.042 --> 00:18:07.583
What nonsense is this?
My son didn't do anything.

184
00:18:07.667 --> 00:18:10.042
Sir. there must be some misunderstanding.

185
00:18:10.125 --> 00:18:12.125
Where are you taking him? I'll go with you.

186
00:18:12.208 --> 00:18:13.875
We have orders to take him alone. sir.

187
00:18:13.958 --> 00:18:16.333
Lieutenant. Lieutenant Fernand de Morcerf.

188
00:18:16.833 --> 00:18:19.167
Tell your friends to let us pass. Lieutenant.

189
00:18:19.250 --> 00:18:20.625
This is a royal order.

190
00:18:22.083 --> 00:18:24.833
- I'll take care of it.
- Please. come with us now. sir.

191
00:18:25.792 --> 00:18:28.792
- Edmond!
- Don't worry. I'll be back. my love!

192
00:19:07.375 --> 00:19:09.625
Edmond Dantés. Mr. Prosecutor.

193
00:19:09.708 --> 00:19:10.875
Leave us.

194
00:19:19.792 --> 00:19:22.833
I've always admired sailors like you.
Mr. Dantes.

195
00:19:23.667 --> 00:19:25.708
Nothing scares me. apart from the sea.

196
00:19:26.375 --> 00:19:29.125
It's an endless abyss.

197
00:19:31.583 --> 00:19:33.292
With its black water.

198
00:19:35.042 --> 00:19:38.750
It feels like a monster is just waiting
to come out and eat you.

199
00:19:41.250 --> 00:19:42.917
What's the charge. Mr. Prosecutor?

200
00:19:43.542 --> 00:19:45.667
Why was I arrested
in the middle of my wedding?

201
00:19:45.750 --> 00:19:48.750
Do you have an enemy. Mr. Dantés?

202
00:19:50.750 --> 00:19:51.917
An enemy?

203
00:19:52.792 --> 00:19:54.292
Yes. or someone who's jealous?

204
00:19:55.042 --> 00:19:56.250
You've been made captain.

205
00:19:56.333 --> 00:19:59.292
You're about to marry one
of the best eligible women in the region.

206
00:20:00.125 --> 00:20:02.792
Someone could be envious.
you know what people are like.

207
00:20:02.875 --> 00:20:04.875
...I don't know.

208
00:20:05.542 --> 00:20:08.625
I had a disagreement
with a crew member recently.

209
00:20:08.708 --> 00:20:10.583
but I don't see what
he could charge me with.

210
00:20:11.875 --> 00:20:13.000
I don't know.

211
00:20:15.708 --> 00:20:18.000
Of being a Napoleonic agent. for example.

212
00:20:18.083 --> 00:20:19.125
I beg your pardon?

213
00:20:20.458 --> 00:20:22.375
T-- That doesn't make any sense.

214
00:20:27.417 --> 00:20:30.792
We found this Bible in your cabin.

215
00:20:32.250 --> 00:20:33.667
This is your Bible. isn't it?

216
00:20:34.458 --> 00:20:36.292
It's got your name on it.

217
00:20:37.667 --> 00:20:39.750
Yes. but that's not a crime.

218
00:20:41.083 --> 00:20:42.083
Indeed.

219
00:20:43.167 --> 00:20:47.375
But we also found
inside of it a mission order...

220
00:20:48.583 --> 00:20:50.792
...signed by Napoleon himself.

221
00:20:51.625 --> 00:20:53.125
And that. you see. is a crime.

222
00:20:53.583 --> 00:20:54.708
Wait. wait!

223
00:20:55.667 --> 00:20:58.917
No. I-- I swear.
I've never seen this letter before!

224
00:20:59.542 --> 00:21:02.125
If you don't have an enemy.
who could have put it there?

225
00:21:05.125 --> 00:21:09.417
Off Cap Corse.
I saved a young woman from drowning.

226
00:21:09.500 --> 00:21:11.750
Did she came to your cabin to thank you?

227
00:21:11.833 --> 00:21:16.625
No. But Captain Danglars locked her there.
and she didn't get out until Marseilles.

228
00:21:16.708 --> 00:21:18.042
You can check.

229
00:21:18.708 --> 00:21:21.875
You can ask Caderousse.
Quartermaster Gaspard Caderousse.

230
00:21:21.958 --> 00:21:24.125
- He can confirm it for you.
- Caderousse?

231
00:21:24.208 --> 00:21:25.208
Yes.

232
00:21:25.958 --> 00:21:28.208
- What do you know about this woman?
- Nothing.

233
00:21:28.958 --> 00:21:30.000
Mr. Dantés.

234
00:21:30.875 --> 00:21:33.167
I've interrogated
many conspirators in my life.

235
00:21:33.250 --> 00:21:34.833
I don't think you're one of them.

236
00:21:35.958 --> 00:21:38.417
I'm happy to help a friend of de Morcerf.

237
00:21:39.250 --> 00:21:40.875
but I need your help as well.

238
00:21:41.958 --> 00:21:43.625
I swear. I don't know anything about her.

239
00:21:47.833 --> 00:21:49.500
She just said her name was Angéle.

240
00:21:50.458 --> 00:21:51.500
That's all.

241
00:21:59.792 --> 00:22:03.250
Did you reveal
this young woman's name to anyone?

242
00:22:04.083 --> 00:22:05.083
No.

243
00:22:07.750 --> 00:22:09.167
Not even to Caderousse?

244
00:22:10.167 --> 00:22:13.167
No. I told no one. I swear on my honor.

245
00:22:14.625 --> 00:22:16.042
Well. you see. Mr. Dantés.

246
00:22:16.833 --> 00:22:17.917
I believe you.

247
00:22:19.958 --> 00:22:23.250
Nevertheless. I'll have
to keep you for a while longer.

248
00:22:23.333 --> 00:22:25.292
while I interrogate the crew.

249
00:22:26.000 --> 00:22:28.667
If he confirms your testimony.
which I'm sure he will.

250
00:22:28.750 --> 00:22:30.333
I'll return you to your fiancée.

251
00:22:30.417 --> 00:22:33.708
who will be delighted
blaming me for this issue.

252
00:22:34.250 --> 00:22:35.542
You can count on it.

253
00:22:39.292 --> 00:22:40.667
Fernand will bring him back.

254
00:22:44.542 --> 00:22:48.375
- I can't take it. I'm going!
- There's nothing you can do that he can't.

255
00:22:49.917 --> 00:22:51.792
You'd be happy if they imprisoned him.

256
00:22:54.250 --> 00:22:56.667
How can you say
such horrible things. Mercédés?

257
00:23:15.667 --> 00:23:19.250
Gérard. Whatever you've heard
about Dantés. I'll vouch for it.

258
00:23:22.500 --> 00:23:24.333
Give us a moment. please. gentlemen.

259
00:23:35.333 --> 00:23:37.292
Fernand. I'm so sorry about your friend.

260
00:23:38.292 --> 00:23:39.500
I know you're close...

261
00:23:41.000 --> 00:23:42.542
...but there's a lot you don't know.

262
00:23:44.542 --> 00:23:47.333
We found an order
from the emperor on his person.

263
00:23:48.583 --> 00:23:51.292
And these crewmen claim
he's one of the emperor's followers.

264
00:23:53.292 --> 00:23:56.292
I think you understand
the seriousness of these accusations.

265
00:23:58.458 --> 00:23:59.625
We were lucky enough to stop him

266
00:23:59.708 --> 00:24:02.500
before he married Mercédés
and damaged her reputation.

267
00:24:03.375 --> 00:24:05.583
But if you're willing to vouch for him.

268
00:24:06.458 --> 00:24:08.583
if you think those two men are lying...

269
00:24:10.875 --> 00:24:14.417
...if you're willing to take that risk.
then I'll let him go.

270
00:24:19.833 --> 00:24:21.042
Just say the word.

271
00:24:26.167 --> 00:24:27.167
No.

272
00:24:31.542 --> 00:24:32.542
No?

273
00:24:38.000 --> 00:24:39.208
He doesn't deserve it.

274
00:24:43.458 --> 00:24:44.708
What doesn't he deserve?

275
00:24:49.083 --> 00:24:51.083
To soil our family's name.

276
00:25:01.250 --> 00:25:02.917
If Dantés betrayed us...

277
00:25:04.792 --> 00:25:06.542
...what will become of him?

278
00:25:07.542 --> 00:25:08.792
I can see to it...

279
00:25:10.208 --> 00:25:13.083
...that no trial will tarnish
the reputation of de Morcerf.

280
00:25:16.958 --> 00:25:18.583
I'm going to need you to testify.

281
00:25:32.292 --> 00:25:33.833
Do you understand?

282
00:25:36.708 --> 00:25:38.083
So keep your mouth shut.

283
00:25:47.750 --> 00:25:49.042
Mr. Dantés.

284
00:25:49.917 --> 00:25:52.458
- Were you able to talk to the prosecutor?
- Yes. sir.

285
00:25:56.875 --> 00:25:58.833
This is a day I'll never forget.

286
00:26:01.500 --> 00:26:03.500
I don't suppose you're taking me home.

287
00:26:03.583 --> 00:26:04.708
No. we're not.

288
00:26:05.542 --> 00:26:06.542
Go ahead.

289
00:26:08.167 --> 00:26:11.333
Wait. what's going on? What's going on?

290
00:26:11.417 --> 00:26:13.292
Let go of me! Call the prosecutor.

291
00:26:13.375 --> 00:26:16.667
I've spoken with the prosecutor!
Call him! Call him!

292
00:26:17.167 --> 00:26:20.792
I'm innocent! I didn't do I.
I'm innocent! Let go of me!

293
00:26:36.750 --> 00:26:38.417
If you were guilty. you'd be hanged!

294
00:26:38.500 --> 00:26:42.583
The only reason I'm taking you
is because you know things. so shut up.

295
00:26:45.333 --> 00:26:46.333
Get up.

296
00:26:59.708 --> 00:27:02.667
Stop. Stop!

297
00:27:11.000 --> 00:27:12.458
Let go of me!

298
00:27:27.625 --> 00:27:30.333
- Where is he?
- I couldn't do anything.

299
00:27:33.417 --> 00:27:34.458
Mercédés.

300
00:27:35.083 --> 00:27:36.125
Let me go.

301
00:27:37.583 --> 00:27:39.000
It wouldn't do any good.

302
00:27:40.250 --> 00:27:42.792
- Mercédés. please!
- Let me--

303
00:28:11.500 --> 00:28:13.083
What's wrong. Victoria?

304
00:28:14.500 --> 00:28:16.375
Aren't you happy to see me?

305
00:28:16.458 --> 00:28:17.625
Your sister is here.

306
00:28:29.333 --> 00:28:31.292
Mademoiselle de Villefort.

307
00:28:32.375 --> 00:28:34.333
clandestinity agrees with you.

308
00:28:35.583 --> 00:28:38.000
I'm sorry I can't return the compliment.

309
00:28:39.750 --> 00:28:41.167
Cognac?

310
00:28:41.250 --> 00:28:43.125
I'm sorry. I'm out of seawater.

311
00:28:45.083 --> 00:28:47.917
That's right.
it's my job to know everything.

312
00:28:49.500 --> 00:28:51.875
In that case. you know Dantés is innocent.

313
00:28:51.958 --> 00:28:53.292
Innocent? Yes.

314
00:28:55.208 --> 00:28:58.042
- Who is truly innocent these days?
- He didn't do anything.

315
00:28:59.208 --> 00:29:00.417
Why did you arrest him?

316
00:29:00.500 --> 00:29:02.792
To save you. What kind of question is that?

317
00:29:02.875 --> 00:29:04.375
Me or your reputation?

318
00:29:06.083 --> 00:29:07.792
We're both in politics.

319
00:29:08.958 --> 00:29:12.583
In politics. you don't remove a man.
you remove an obstacle.

320
00:29:13.208 --> 00:29:16.542
I knew how cruelly
you practiced your job as a royalist.

321
00:29:16.625 --> 00:29:19.083
but I hoped you'd do it honestly.

322
00:29:19.167 --> 00:29:20.833
Since you're so honest.

323
00:29:20.917 --> 00:29:22.833
why don't you turn yourself in for him?

324
00:29:22.917 --> 00:29:24.500
Oh. I will. Gérard.

325
00:29:25.500 --> 00:29:27.417
If you won't save him. I will.

326
00:29:28.250 --> 00:29:31.292
I think you'd rather
people didn't know about me.

327
00:29:31.375 --> 00:29:36.125
and Victoria. your mistress.
and your unborn child.

328
00:29:46.292 --> 00:29:47.583
That's what I thought.

329
00:30:19.917 --> 00:30:20.917
Alive?

330
00:30:22.458 --> 00:30:23.750
Alive.

331
00:30:37.708 --> 00:30:38.708
Alive?

332
00:30:39.667 --> 00:30:40.833
Alive.

333
00:30:49.167 --> 00:30:50.167
Alive?

334
00:30:51.542 --> 00:30:52.542
Alive.

335
00:32:14.833 --> 00:32:17.333
Right. I-- I'm hearing...

336
00:32:18.042 --> 00:32:21.417
Who... Who exactly...

337
00:33:16.167 --> 00:33:18.833
Someone's there? Someone's there!

338
00:33:26.458 --> 00:33:29.000
Someone's there!

339
00:33:31.958 --> 00:33:33.167
Someone's there!

340
00:33:34.250 --> 00:33:36.083
Someone's there...

341
00:33:40.083 --> 00:33:41.083
Someone--

342
00:33:53.500 --> 00:33:54.625
Who are you?

343
00:33:55.292 --> 00:33:57.833
I-- Dantés. Edmond Dantés.

344
00:33:59.208 --> 00:34:00.458
How old are you?

345
00:34:01.833 --> 00:34:04.042
You sound like a young man.

346
00:34:04.125 --> 00:34:06.125
Ha}

347
00:34:07.667 --> 00:34:08.917
I don't know.

348
00:34:09.583 --> 00:34:12.708
I was 22... when they locked me up.

349
00:34:14.042 --> 00:34:16.167
May 16th. 1815.

350
00:34:17.625 --> 00:34:19.125
That was four years ago.

351
00:34:22.125 --> 00:34:23.458
You're 26.

352
00:34:26.542 --> 00:34:27.542
Four years?

353
00:34:32.833 --> 00:34:35.250
And you? Who are you?

354
00:34:37.167 --> 00:34:38.292
A prisoner.

355
00:34:40.375 --> 00:34:41.375
Like you.

356
00:34:42.083 --> 00:34:43.292
For how long?

357
00:34:44.708 --> 00:34:46.625
- Hush.
- What is it?

358
00:34:46.708 --> 00:34:49.792
- They're coming.
- Wait. Don't leave me.

359
00:34:49.875 --> 00:34:51.875
Who are you? At least tell me your name.

360
00:34:52.625 --> 00:34:54.375
- Alive?
- Your name!

361
00:34:54.458 --> 00:34:55.458
Alive.

362
00:35:01.000 --> 00:35:02.833
Thirty-four. alive?

363
00:35:05.208 --> 00:35:06.208
Alive.

364
00:37:21.542 --> 00:37:23.000
I was waiting for you.

365
00:37:30.958 --> 00:37:33.083
Do you really think we can get out of here?

366
00:37:33.792 --> 00:37:36.292
I've dug 30 meters in six years...

367
00:37:36.375 --> 00:37:39.292
to get around your cell
and reach the outside.

368
00:37:39.917 --> 00:37:42.083
We'll have to dig twice as long.

369
00:37:43.125 --> 00:37:44.417
Twelve years?

370
00:37:44.500 --> 00:37:48.000
Maybe a little less...
now that there are two of us.

371
00:37:49.958 --> 00:37:52.500
Why? Do you have other plans?

372
00:37:56.333 --> 00:37:57.333
No.

373
00:37:59.042 --> 00:38:01.708
I am Abbot Faria.

374
00:38:05.625 --> 00:38:06.792
Edmond Dantés.

375
00:38:31.917 --> 00:38:33.833
You had never seen that letter?

376
00:38:35.250 --> 00:38:36.833
No. I hadn't.

377
00:38:41.750 --> 00:38:44.875
And you. do you know why you're here?

378
00:38:47.417 --> 00:38:48.500
Yes.

379
00:38:52.833 --> 00:38:55.458
They wanted to silence you.
but they wanted me to talk.

380
00:38:58.958 --> 00:39:01.833
I only confide in trusted people.

381
00:39:05.000 --> 00:39:07.208
I choose whom I confide in.

382
00:39:08.167 --> 00:39:09.500
You don't speak Italian?

383
00:39:12.042 --> 00:39:16.125
- No.
- English. Arabic. Latin. Greek? No?

384
00:39:17.667 --> 00:39:19.042
No. I only know the sea.

385
00:39:21.458 --> 00:39:23.000
I could teach you. if you want.

386
00:39:24.958 --> 00:39:27.333
With patience and willpower. in...

387
00:39:29.542 --> 00:39:31.917
...Six or seven years.
you'll know everything I know.

388
00:39:34.500 --> 00:39:38.500
History. philosophy. mathematics.

389
00:39:39.250 --> 00:39:41.833
they're all weapons.

390
00:39:43.333 --> 00:39:45.708
They have as much power to free you as this.

391
00:40:50.917 --> 00:40:55.542
What's the first thing you'll do...
if we get out of here?

392
00:40:58.417 --> 00:40:59.792
I'll find Mercédés.

393
00:41:02.667 --> 00:41:04.542
What will you do if she didn't wait for you?

394
00:41:08.208 --> 00:41:09.833
Then I'll have nothing left.

395
00:41:10.875 --> 00:41:13.042
I'll tell you a story. Edmond.

396
00:41:16.417 --> 00:41:21.042
700 years ago. in Jerusalem.
during the first Crusade...

397
00:41:22.625 --> 00:41:25.375
...the knights entrusted
with protecting the tomb of Christ

398
00:41:25.458 --> 00:41:27.458
created the Order of the Templars.

399
00:41:28.750 --> 00:41:32.958
On the first day. there were only
a few of them. but they had great faith.

400
00:41:35.292 --> 00:41:37.625
With their victories.

401
00:41:38.083 --> 00:41:40.167
the order amassed a fortune.

402
00:41:42.292 --> 00:41:43.583
A significant one.

403
00:41:44.792 --> 00:41:47.750
Sig-- significant.

404
00:41:49.042 --> 00:41:52.833
The greatest treasure
the earth has ever seen.

405
00:41:54.292 --> 00:41:55.292
And...

406
00:41:56.958 --> 00:41:58.042
...over time...

407
00:41:59.542 --> 00:42:02.458
their power and wealth made others envious.

408
00:42:03.292 --> 00:42:07.875
On Friday. October 13th. 1307.
the King of France. Philip the Bel.

409
00:42:07.958 --> 00:42:11.542
orders their arrest
and confiscates their possessions.

410
00:42:13.667 --> 00:42:16.333
But no one ever found the treasure.

411
00:42:20.625 --> 00:42:21.750
Do you know...

412
00:42:23.625 --> 00:42:26.833
...what those knights did
with that enormous fortune?

413
00:42:28.625 --> 00:42:30.250
- No.
- Nothing.

414
00:42:31.917 --> 00:42:33.958
Edmond. they did nothing.

415
00:42:34.792 --> 00:42:36.750
They were too busy gnawing at themselves.

416
00:42:38.083 --> 00:42:41.000
Punishing those who betrayed them.

417
00:42:41.958 --> 00:42:44.500
They all died. one by one.

418
00:42:46.333 --> 00:42:47.917
Well. almost all of them.

419
00:42:51.083 --> 00:42:54.375
The last of them was Cardinal Spada.

420
00:42:56.208 --> 00:43:00.792
At the end of his life. he took refuge
on the Isle of Monte Cristo.

421
00:43:02.375 --> 00:43:04.833
He had enough time to train one last knight.

422
00:43:07.292 --> 00:43:11.292
A young man named Giuseppe Faria.

423
00:43:15.417 --> 00:43:17.833
I'm the last one left. Edmond.

424
00:43:20.375 --> 00:43:22.958
And I know where the treasure is.

425
00:43:26.083 --> 00:43:29.000
Half of it is yours now.

426
00:43:30.667 --> 00:43:32.667
But what will you do with all this wealth?

427
00:43:36.708 --> 00:43:38.000
Will you do good?

428
00:43:39.917 --> 00:43:42.333
Or will you let your heart
be overcome with hate?

429
00:44:34.167 --> 00:44:35.417
I'll go empty the bag.

430
00:44:38.958 --> 00:44:39.958
Edmond.

431
00:44:45.792 --> 00:44:48.792
It's salty. The water is salty.

432
00:44:50.792 --> 00:44:53.667
We're almost there.
It's just a matter of days.

433
00:45:00.792 --> 00:45:02.500
We're almost there!

434
00:45:04.542 --> 00:45:05.542
I'll be right back.

435
00:45:10.417 --> 00:45:12.000
Come back. Abbot. come back!

436
00:45:21.125 --> 00:45:22.125
Abbot?

437
00:45:26.958 --> 00:45:28.958
Abbot? Abbot!

438
00:45:49.500 --> 00:45:51.708
- There.
- Edmond--

439
00:45:51.792 --> 00:45:55.542
No. don't talk.
I'll call for help. I'll call--

440
00:45:55.625 --> 00:45:58.208
No. It's too late.

441
00:46:00.667 --> 00:46:02.417
Don't be sad.

442
00:46:05.958 --> 00:46:09.458
You have been the only solace in my life.

443
00:46:10.167 --> 00:46:12.250
God sent you to me.

444
00:46:13.583 --> 00:46:16.042
Maybe a little late.

445
00:46:20.042 --> 00:46:21.875
I'm not crazy.

446
00:46:23.458 --> 00:46:24.625
I know.

447
00:46:26.250 --> 00:46:27.958
The treasure is real.

448
00:46:29.708 --> 00:46:31.167
You know where to find it.

449
00:46:32.208 --> 00:46:35.667
- We can look for it together.
- Don't-- don't forget.

450
00:46:36.417 --> 00:46:37.750
Monte Cristo!

451
00:46:39.417 --> 00:46:41.083
Monte Cristo...

452
00:46:45.042 --> 00:46:47.208
Abbot. Abbot!

453
00:46:49.542 --> 00:46:50.542
Abbot!

454
00:46:51.917 --> 00:46:53.042
Don't leave me.

455
00:46:54.125 --> 00:46:55.250
Don't leave me!

456
00:46:57.292 --> 00:46:58.583
Don't leave me.

457
00:47:19.292 --> 00:47:21.458
- Alive?
- Alive.

458
00:47:28.125 --> 00:47:29.208
Alive?

459
00:47:31.208 --> 00:47:32.292
Number 17.

460
00:47:34.542 --> 00:47:35.625
Hey. 17!

461
00:47:59.333 --> 00:48:00.333
Abbot?

462
00:48:26.917 --> 00:48:28.000
Hey. Abbot?

463
00:48:39.833 --> 00:48:42.458
Hey! He's dead! Throw me a bag.

464
00:49:42.417 --> 00:49:44.458
- Who is it?
- The Abbot.

465
00:49:57.792 --> 00:49:58.792
Alive?

466
00:49:59.833 --> 00:50:00.833
Alive.

467
00:50:21.958 --> 00:50:22.958
Alive?

468
00:50:31.208 --> 00:50:32.208
Alive?

469
00:51:00.000 --> 00:51:02.500
Come on. get up. Get up!

470
00:51:05.500 --> 00:51:06.708
I said. get up!

471
00:51:11.833 --> 00:51:12.917
On alert!

472
00:51:17.250 --> 00:51:19.542
- One...
- On alert!

473
00:51:20.083 --> 00:51:21.167
...two...

474
00:51:21.750 --> 00:51:23.083
Alert!

475
00:51:23.167 --> 00:51:24.750
...and three!

476
00:54:46.542 --> 00:54:49.458
Hey! You have no business being here!
Leave at once!

477
00:54:50.583 --> 00:54:51.667
I came to see Louis.

478
00:54:52.250 --> 00:54:53.375
Louis Dantés.

479
00:54:53.792 --> 00:54:55.042
You knew Louis?

480
00:54:55.917 --> 00:54:56.917
Yes.

481
00:54:57.750 --> 00:54:59.292
We buried poor old Louis.

482
00:55:00.625 --> 00:55:02.000
A long time ago. my boy.

483
00:55:06.375 --> 00:55:08.083
No. it can't be.

484
00:55:08.167 --> 00:55:10.583
He starved himself to death
after his son died.

485
00:55:12.333 --> 00:55:13.667
He wanted to be with him again.

486
00:55:18.917 --> 00:55:20.333
But his...

487
00:55:20.417 --> 00:55:21.958
His son isn't dead.

488
00:55:24.083 --> 00:55:25.292
I'm sorry.

489
00:55:31.833 --> 00:55:33.458
Were you a sailor too?

490
00:55:34.542 --> 00:55:35.542
Yes.

491
00:55:36.875 --> 00:55:40.083
I'll feed you. but after that. you're off.

492
00:55:46.208 --> 00:55:47.542
Mercéd--

493
00:55:47.625 --> 00:55:51.208
Mercédés and Fernand de Morcerf.

494
00:55:51.750 --> 00:55:54.125
It's been seven or eight years
since they last came.

495
00:55:54.958 --> 00:55:57.458
They've been living in Paris
since their son was born.

496
00:56:00.625 --> 00:56:01.750
You're too late.

497
00:57:00.167 --> 00:57:04.667
Avoid the Ligurian Sea.
with its relentless patrols.

498
00:57:05.375 --> 00:57:07.333
Set a course for Sardinia.

499
00:57:09.042 --> 00:57:12.458
You can make port
at Santa Teresa di Gallura.

500
00:57:13.375 --> 00:57:18.208
The Isle of Monte Cristo lies
to the west of the Tuscan Archipelago.

501
00:57:39.042 --> 00:57:40.875
You'll land at the southern tip.

502
00:57:41.625 --> 00:57:46.333
I know you'll be overwhelmed
by its austere beauty.

503
00:57:47.875 --> 00:57:51.417
I envy you for seeing it for the first time.

504
00:57:53.000 --> 00:57:55.417
There it is.

505
00:57:57.250 --> 00:58:00.167
The burial plot of the famous De Spada family.

506
00:58:00.583 --> 00:58:01.917
The rest. Edmond...

507
00:58:03.583 --> 00:58:04.875
...Is your story.

508
00:58:07.458 --> 00:58:12.750
The story of a man who has
the whole world in the palm of his hand.

509
01:00:58.000 --> 01:01:01.083
- Come on. I'll pay you tomorrow.
- No.

510
01:01:02.167 --> 01:01:04.333
Mr. Caderousse is my friend.

511
01:01:15.083 --> 01:01:19.458
On his deathbed.
Edmond Dantés asked me to share it

512
01:01:19.542 --> 01:01:21.375
with the people he cared about.

513
01:01:24.958 --> 01:01:29.042
He believed he'd been turned in
by a man named Danglars.

514
01:01:29.792 --> 01:01:33.625
But he was convinced there were
two men who remained loyal to him.

515
01:01:34.625 --> 01:01:38.750
He told me that one of them
was Gaspard Caderousse.

516
01:01:38.833 --> 01:01:41.958
and the other was Fernand de Morcerf.

517
01:01:44.167 --> 01:01:47.500
You can keep your diamond.
None of us deserve anything.

518
01:01:48.625 --> 01:01:50.125
Wait. my son.

519
01:01:50.917 --> 01:01:54.000
If I tell you what I know.
everyone will know it came from me.

520
01:01:54.083 --> 01:01:56.083
And these people are rich and powerful.

521
01:01:56.792 --> 01:01:58.375
There's nothing to be afraid of.

522
01:01:58.917 --> 01:02:01.542
I'm bound by the Seal of Confession.

523
01:02:02.125 --> 01:02:03.500
Please. sit.

524
01:02:12.333 --> 01:02:15.958
Dantés was right about Danglars.
He's the one who reported him.

525
01:02:18.500 --> 01:02:22.500
But Fernand de Morcerf... was his friend.

526
01:02:24.500 --> 01:02:27.083
He was in love with his fiancée.

527
01:02:28.250 --> 01:02:32.167
For Mercédés' sake. he sacrificed Edmond.

528
01:02:38.708 --> 01:02:42.042
He'll live. But he'll be dead to the world.

529
01:02:46.542 --> 01:02:49.375
The only one who deserves
Dantés' affection is Morrel.

530
01:02:50.708 --> 01:02:51.833
The ship owner.

531
01:02:53.167 --> 01:02:55.375
He's the only one
who fought to get him released.

532
01:02:56.333 --> 01:02:59.083
But he too was given little thanks.

533
01:03:00.042 --> 01:03:01.583
After Dantés' arrest.

534
01:03:02.083 --> 01:03:04.542
he had no choice but to bring
Danglars back as captain.

535
01:03:05.083 --> 01:03:06.875
But Danglars also betrayed him.

536
01:03:07.792 --> 01:03:09.708
He made half his fleet disappear.

537
01:03:10.250 --> 01:03:12.125
Said it was stolen by pirates.

538
01:03:13.583 --> 01:03:16.375
Ruined. Morrel had to sell the company.

539
01:03:17.167 --> 01:03:19.417
And guess who bought it back for pennies?

540
01:03:20.458 --> 01:03:21.583
Danglars.

541
01:03:22.583 --> 01:03:25.583
Two months later.
the boats reappeared miraculously.

542
01:03:26.917 --> 01:03:29.375
The prosecutor. Villefort. didn't do a thing.

543
01:03:29.917 --> 01:03:32.083
Well. both of them shared a secret.

544
01:03:33.917 --> 01:03:38.458
Victoria. Villefort's mistress.
she had become Mrs. Danglars.

545
01:03:40.917 --> 01:03:42.167
She's a baroness now.

546
01:03:43.250 --> 01:03:45.750
Morrel died a poor man.

547
01:03:49.333 --> 01:03:52.083
And what about you. Mr. Caderousse?

548
01:03:52.875 --> 01:03:53.875
You...

549
01:03:55.458 --> 01:03:56.833
What was I to do...

550
01:03:57.875 --> 01:04:00.375
against a captain. a count. and a prosecutor?

551
01:04:03.167 --> 01:04:04.750
If I had been braver.

552
01:04:05.667 --> 01:04:07.417
I probably would have ended up like her.

553
01:04:08.458 --> 01:04:09.458
Her?

554
01:04:10.667 --> 01:04:11.667
Angéle.

555
01:04:15.417 --> 01:04:18.042
She went to see her brother.
hoping to save Dantes.

556
01:04:18.125 --> 01:04:21.458
I got rid of Dantés for you.
now you get rid of her.

557
01:04:23.333 --> 01:04:26.125
See? I have friends too.

558
01:04:30.333 --> 01:04:32.000
What happened?

559
01:04:33.042 --> 01:04:34.417
Was she killed?

560
01:04:35.875 --> 01:04:37.333
She would have suffered less.

561
01:04:38.417 --> 01:04:40.250
But Danglars had other plans for her.

562
01:04:41.000 --> 01:04:44.500
He sold her to the Maillard brothers.
the masters of the brothel of Toulon.

563
01:04:45.250 --> 01:04:48.417
The girl was pretty.
he got a good price for her.

564
01:04:50.417 --> 01:04:52.542
You knew everything and did nothing.

565
01:04:54.417 --> 01:04:55.792
I'm ashamed. Father.

566
01:04:58.333 --> 01:05:02.458
One day. I'll come back and give you
a chance to redeem yourself.

567
01:05:20.333 --> 01:05:22.667
I no longer come to pray for you
or to find you.

568
01:05:23.625 --> 01:05:25.250
but only to warn you.

569
01:05:26.500 --> 01:05:28.250
I'm going to do what you couldn't.

570
01:05:29.792 --> 01:05:33.042
From now on.
I will reward and I will punish.

571
01:06:02.542 --> 01:06:04.208
Can I do anything for you. sir?

572
01:06:40.000 --> 01:06:41.167
Who are you?

573
01:07:00.042 --> 01:07:03.000
Years ago. you told me...

574
01:07:04.750 --> 01:07:07.500
..."I won't forget your courage.
but you must forget my name."

575
01:07:10.167 --> 01:07:14.125
Well. I haven't forgotten your name
or your courage.

576
01:07:18.125 --> 01:07:19.667
Dantés.

577
01:07:25.625 --> 01:07:27.708
I've come to save you. Angéle.

578
01:07:31.375 --> 01:07:33.000
It's too late for me.

579
01:07:36.167 --> 01:07:38.167
But you can save the child.

580
01:07:40.167 --> 01:07:41.208
The child?

581
01:07:52.875 --> 01:07:54.667
When I first arrived here...

582
01:07:56.333 --> 01:07:58.167
...there was only one thing on my mind.

583
01:08:00.500 --> 01:08:02.292
I wanted revenge on my brother.

584
01:08:03.625 --> 01:08:07.583
For weeks.
I tried to find a way to escape.

585
01:08:10.292 --> 01:08:13.042
One day. the opportunity presented itself.
I ran away.

586
01:08:15.417 --> 01:08:16.667
With a client.

587
01:08:19.208 --> 01:08:20.625
A Parisian draper.

588
01:08:22.958 --> 01:08:25.458
I knew Gérard was appointed there.

589
01:08:27.333 --> 01:08:31.875
I tracked down Victoria. his mistress.

590
01:08:33.542 --> 01:08:36.375
I wanted to pick up
where the story left off.

591
01:08:40.292 --> 01:08:42.042
It was freezing cold.

592
01:08:46.583 --> 01:08:50.500
That night. Gérard was supposed to die.

593
01:08:52.125 --> 01:08:53.458
Nothing could stop me.

594
01:08:55.750 --> 01:08:58.417
I can still feel the knife in my hand.

595
01:09:01.083 --> 01:09:02.667
But nothing went as planned.

596
01:09:10.417 --> 01:09:13.792
I heard a scream. Victoria's scream.

597
01:09:14.875 --> 01:09:18.750
When Gérard went out into the garden.
he was carrying a chest.

598
01:09:19.583 --> 01:09:20.750
I followed him.

599
01:09:32.083 --> 01:09:37.500
! moved closer. and I heard
the muffled screams of a baby.

600
01:09:47.583 --> 01:09:48.958
I couldn't leave him.

601
01:09:50.833 --> 01:09:53.167
He still had his mother's blood on his body.

602
01:10:00.667 --> 01:10:02.458
Between revenge and life...

603
01:10:04.833 --> 01:10:06.333
...I chose life.

604
01:10:12.167 --> 01:10:13.708
I ran away with him.

605
01:10:15.958 --> 01:10:17.958
I didn't know anyone in Paris.

606
01:10:20.333 --> 01:10:22.417
So. I went back to my draper.

607
01:10:25.083 --> 01:10:27.458
But the Maillard brothers had found him...

608
01:10:29.083 --> 01:10:30.375
...and were waiting for me.

609
01:10:38.708 --> 01:10:39.833
Angéle...

610
01:10:43.333 --> 01:10:44.542
...what happened to the baby?

611
01:11:17.583 --> 01:11:18.708
Hello. André.

612
01:11:20.208 --> 01:11:23.208
- Angéle asked me to come and get you.
- Why?

613
01:11:25.708 --> 01:11:26.750
She's dying.

614
01:11:27.958 --> 01:11:30.542
I'll take you to her so you can say goodbye.

615
01:11:33.750 --> 01:11:35.000
And then we'll leave.

616
01:11:37.083 --> 01:11:40.542
We'll take all the time we need to be ready.

617
01:11:42.000 --> 01:11:43.000
Ready for what?

618
01:11:44.458 --> 01:11:46.458
Revenge. André.

619
01:11:49.083 --> 01:11:51.417
To take revenge on the three men
who stole her life.

620
01:11:52.000 --> 01:11:54.292
yours. and mine.

621
01:11:56.417 --> 01:11:57.542
I want to kill them.

622
01:11:58.708 --> 01:12:00.958
That would be too easy. Too merciful.

623
01:12:03.292 --> 01:12:04.292
No.

624
01:12:06.333 --> 01:12:07.833
We must cut out their hearts.

625
01:12:10.625 --> 01:12:11.750
Who are you?

626
01:12:13.708 --> 01:12:15.625
I'm the Count of Monte Cristo.

627
01:12:24.208 --> 01:12:27.375
Today. the General de Morcerf
has decided to leave the army

628
01:12:27.458 --> 01:12:30.625
and dedicate his life to politics.
to the Chamber of Peers.

629
01:12:31.250 --> 01:12:36.625
The French army is losing a great soldier.
but France is gaining a great man.

630
01:12:37.792 --> 01:12:42.917
Fernand de Morcerf fought at the Moskva River.
in Leipzig. in Turkey.

631
01:12:43.000 --> 01:12:47.208
Everywhere. at great risk to his life.
he defended the kingdom of France.

632
01:12:49.292 --> 01:12:53.167
Fernand paid in his own flesh
the price of his pledge

633
01:12:53.250 --> 01:12:54.958
and the honor of his word.

634
01:12:55.625 --> 01:12:58.667
Ten years ago. when France's ally.

635
01:12:59.250 --> 01:13:02.917
Ali Pasha of Yanina.
was under siege from Turkish troops.

636
01:13:03.000 --> 01:13:06.208
Colonel de Morcerf went all out.

637
01:13:07.125 --> 01:13:10.208
At the head of a squadron of valiant soldiers.

638
01:13:10.292 --> 01:13:15.875
he broke through the Ottomans' lines
to lend a hand to his ally.

639
01:13:15.958 --> 01:13:20.875
Unfortunately. this act
of foolish courage wasn't enough...

640
01:13:21.833 --> 01:13:26.042
...but as every Frenchman knows.
we don't fight in hopes of success.

641
01:13:26.125 --> 01:13:29.875
no. it's much more beautiful when it's hopeless.

642
01:14:16.833 --> 01:14:17.875
Better now?

643
01:14:23.083 --> 01:14:26.042
You weren't very considerate
with Eugenie Danglars.

644
01:14:26.667 --> 01:14:27.583
Father--

645
01:14:27.667 --> 01:14:30.208
She'll have a dowry of two million
on her wedding day.

646
01:14:30.292 --> 01:14:32.125
- Fernand!
- So it's not Eugénie

647
01:14:32.208 --> 01:14:34.667
I have to worry about so much as her fortune.

648
01:14:34.750 --> 01:14:37.833
Believe me. it's better to have
one less medal and one more zero.

649
01:14:40.708 --> 01:14:44.667
Our son is a man of his time.
He's a romantic who believes--

650
01:15:18.458 --> 01:15:19.583
Take the medal.

651
01:16:32.042 --> 01:16:33.167
Enough.

652
01:17:58.083 --> 01:18:01.375
Gentlemen. had I known of your visit.
I would have prepared myself for it.

653
01:18:03.792 --> 01:18:07.917
Gentlemen. had I known of your visit.
I would have prepared myself for it.

654
01:19:33.417 --> 01:19:35.208
Stop! Get out!

655
01:19:37.208 --> 01:19:38.250
Gentlemen...

656
01:19:39.667 --> 01:19:42.333
...had I known of your visit.
I would have prepared myself.

657
01:19:42.417 --> 01:19:45.750
I'm sorry to welcome you in a makeshift home.

658
01:19:46.625 --> 01:19:48.458
I've only been in France for a few weeks.

659
01:19:49.000 --> 01:19:52.625
I'm sorry to bother you at home.
but our family can't thank you enough

660
01:19:52.708 --> 01:19:54.083
for saving Albert's life.

661
01:19:55.042 --> 01:19:58.208
The way he fought. I'm sure
he would have done the same for me.

662
01:19:58.792 --> 01:20:00.542
Count. I owe you my life.

663
01:20:02.792 --> 01:20:05.500
I'm glad to see you
on your feet again. young man.

664
01:20:07.917 --> 01:20:10.583
I had it fixed. The handle was cracked.

665
01:20:11.417 --> 01:20:12.833
Well. it's yours now.

666
01:20:14.708 --> 01:20:18.875
I'm very grateful. Count. but I can't accept it.

667
01:20:18.958 --> 01:20:21.958
I'm already in your debt
and I don't know how to repay you.

668
01:20:28.000 --> 01:20:29.208
Do you like guns?

669
01:20:33.125 --> 01:20:34.333
Please. follow me.

670
01:20:49.708 --> 01:20:53.542
That's one of my finest pieces.
An Ottoman-style pistol.

671
01:20:54.958 --> 01:20:57.750
The iron under guard on this cannon.
decorated with foliage.

672
01:20:58.250 --> 01:21:01.625
means it was made in Europe.

673
01:21:02.667 --> 01:21:06.292
It was made in Venice.
You're quite the connoisseur.

674
01:21:07.500 --> 01:21:11.125
My father fought against
Sultan Curci with Ali Pasha.

675
01:21:11.208 --> 01:21:12.375
Morcerf.

676
01:21:13.542 --> 01:21:17.250
You are the famous General de Morcerf.
I'm very impressed.

677
01:21:17.958 --> 01:21:19.708
Would you do me the honor of trying it?

678
01:21:19.792 --> 01:21:22.792
Unfortunately.
I have to get back to the Chamber.

679
01:21:22.875 --> 01:21:25.583
- But some other time. I'd be happy to.
- It won't take long.

680
01:21:53.958 --> 01:21:56.333
You've earned your reputation. General.

681
01:21:57.750 --> 01:22:00.125
We'll have to change the target for you. Albert.

682
01:22:09.833 --> 01:22:12.500
Remind me never to challenge you to a duel.

683
01:22:14.292 --> 01:22:16.958
I appreciate you leaving your son
with me for a few hours.

684
01:22:17.042 --> 01:22:20.542
I can't wait to find out more
about the man fate has placed in my path.

685
01:22:21.208 --> 01:22:23.458
I'm taking part
in Baron Danglars' hunt on Sunday.

686
01:22:23.542 --> 01:22:24.833
Why don't you join us?

687
01:22:25.750 --> 01:22:29.833
I'd love to. but I can't.
I must greet the son of Prince Cavalcanti.

688
01:22:29.917 --> 01:22:32.875
Why don't you both come?
There will be enough stags for everyone.

689
01:22:34.417 --> 01:22:35.458
See you soon.

690
01:22:36.333 --> 01:22:37.458
See you Sunday. I hope.

691
01:22:40.417 --> 01:22:41.458
Is everything alright?

692
01:22:44.333 --> 01:22:48.583
My Ottoman adventure left me
with a small metal memento.

693
01:24:53.208 --> 01:24:55.292
You prefer singing to weapons?

694
01:25:00.375 --> 01:25:01.375
Follow me.

695
01:25:08.208 --> 01:25:09.958
I beg your pardon. Count.

696
01:25:10.042 --> 01:25:12.833
I meant no disrespect to your wife.

697
01:25:14.208 --> 01:25:15.625
Haydée isn't my wife.

698
01:25:16.167 --> 01:25:17.292
She's my goddaughter.

699
01:25:18.250 --> 01:25:19.250
After you.

700
01:25:20.125 --> 01:25:21.167
Haydée.

701
01:25:22.583 --> 01:25:23.792
What a wonderful name.

702
01:25:24.625 --> 01:25:26.583
It's a pretty common name in Greece.

703
01:25:27.375 --> 01:25:31.875
It could be translated
as "modesty" or "innocence."

704
01:25:38.458 --> 01:25:40.875
May I ask you to introduce me to Haydée?

705
01:25:44.083 --> 01:25:46.250
You seem like a very trustworthy young man.

706
01:25:46.917 --> 01:25:48.333
I'll introduce you.

707
01:25:48.417 --> 01:25:50.667
But before I do so.
you must promise me something.

708
01:25:50.750 --> 01:25:51.917
I'll do it now.

709
01:25:53.375 --> 01:25:54.458
I'm not joking.

710
01:25:57.208 --> 01:25:59.083
You must never try to seduce her.

711
01:26:00.792 --> 01:26:02.500
So you think I'm dangerous?

712
01:26:03.292 --> 01:26:04.292
No.

713
01:26:05.292 --> 01:26:06.417
But she is.

714
01:26:08.417 --> 01:26:10.167
If you don't keep your promise.

715
01:26:10.875 --> 01:26:13.542
she'll break your heart. and hers.

716
01:26:14.417 --> 01:26:17.167
But she's not ready to love yet.

717
01:26:17.875 --> 01:26:21.000
The secret of her enchanting voice
lies in her past.

718
01:26:21.083 --> 01:26:22.792
After her father was murdered.

719
01:26:22.875 --> 01:26:25.292
she was sold to a Viach tribe from the Balkans.

720
01:26:26.167 --> 01:26:29.042
That's when I met her and took her in.

721
01:26:29.125 --> 01:26:34.083
You know. some sorrows
and wounds take years to heal.

722
01:26:35.167 --> 01:26:37.625
They leave a veil over our souls.

723
01:26:40.417 --> 01:26:43.333
Don't ever try to lift that veil. Albert.

724
01:26:46.333 --> 01:26:47.333
I promise.

725
01:26:50.292 --> 01:26:51.208
Good.

726
01:26:51.292 --> 01:26:53.583
You'll walk softly.
and never give us so much as a glance.

727
01:26:54.083 --> 01:26:55.750
Turn only when I call for you.

728
01:26:59.125 --> 01:27:00.208
Haydée.

729
01:27:04.792 --> 01:27:06.083
Albert de Morcerf.

730
01:27:06.167 --> 01:27:09.542
- may I introduce Haydée.
- Pleasure to meet you. sir.

731
01:27:09.833 --> 01:27:11.208
Pleasure to meet you. sir.

732
01:27:13.917 --> 01:27:15.250
It's a pleasure to meet you. miss.

733
01:27:15.333 --> 01:27:17.167
And if he doesn't want to meet me?

734
01:27:17.917 --> 01:27:19.042
He will.

735
01:27:20.792 --> 01:27:24.625
Sit up straight! From now on.
sitting up straight is survival.

736
01:27:24.708 --> 01:27:27.625
Making it look like
you didn't grow up poor is survival.

737
01:27:27.708 --> 01:27:30.292
Do you understand why? Why is that. André?

738
01:27:31.167 --> 01:27:33.417
Because I am Prince Andrea Cavalcanti.

739
01:27:34.875 --> 01:27:36.958
Doesn't Cavalcanti mean goat in Spanish?

740
01:27:37.042 --> 01:27:38.958
- What?
- Don't look so surprised. "What?"

741
01:27:39.042 --> 01:27:40.958
Do you hear me saying "what"? Start over.

742
01:27:43.167 --> 01:27:45.625
I'm Prince Andrea Cavalcanti.

743
01:27:46.208 --> 01:27:48.875
But you don't have an accent. Prince.
how come?

744
01:27:49.625 --> 01:27:53.208
I had a very strict teacher
who beat my accent out of me.

745
01:27:53.833 --> 01:27:55.833
That's rude. Your elbows.

746
01:28:00.125 --> 01:28:02.333
Dear Count. it's a pleasure to meet you.

747
01:28:02.833 --> 01:28:04.375
Let me tell you something.

748
01:28:04.458 --> 01:28:06.917
I'm still completely unfamiliar with French life.

749
01:28:07.000 --> 01:28:12.042
So. please forgive me in advance if my manners
may seem too Slavic. Neapolitan. or Arab.

750
01:28:46.625 --> 01:28:49.083
My friends. may I present
the Count of Monte Cristo

751
01:28:49.167 --> 01:28:51.083
and Prince Andrea Cavalcanti.

752
01:28:52.750 --> 01:28:54.375
- Gentlemen.
- Count.

753
01:28:56.167 --> 01:28:57.250
Prince.

754
01:28:58.125 --> 01:29:02.875
Meeting your father. as upsetting as it may be.
can't distract you from your goal.

755
01:29:02.958 --> 01:29:05.792
Baron Danglars made his fortune
in the slave trade

756
01:29:05.875 --> 01:29:08.083
thanks to the ships he stole from Morrel.

757
01:29:08.167 --> 01:29:10.208
Your reputation precedes you. Count.

758
01:29:10.292 --> 01:29:15.458
Don't be fooled by his smile. He's brutal.
And he not only knows it. he takes pride in it.

759
01:29:15.542 --> 01:29:16.792
May I make a confession?

760
01:29:17.333 --> 01:29:19.750
I'm still completely unfamiliar with French life.

761
01:29:19.833 --> 01:29:22.417
So. please forgive me in advance

762
01:29:22.500 --> 01:29:26.792
if my manners seem
too Slavic. Neapolitan. or Arab.

763
01:29:27.375 --> 01:29:30.250
When you're rich.
you can never be too much of anything.

764
01:29:30.333 --> 01:29:32.708
- His weakness is his daughter.
- Prince.

765
01:29:34.042 --> 01:29:35.375
- Baron.
- Eugénie.

766
01:29:35.458 --> 01:29:37.500
- The playground isn't so bad.
- It's perfect.

767
01:29:38.000 --> 01:29:39.917
Then let's go. Mount up. gentlemen.

768
01:31:15.250 --> 01:31:16.458
Do us the honors. Count.

769
01:31:18.083 --> 01:31:22.375
I'm grateful. Baron.
but I took an oath a long time ago.

770
01:31:22.458 --> 01:31:24.042
I only kill in self-defense.

771
01:31:24.750 --> 01:31:26.750
Please let me defend you. Count.

772
01:31:28.917 --> 01:31:29.917
Very well.

773
01:31:30.958 --> 01:31:31.958
Prince.

774
01:31:33.333 --> 01:31:34.458
You do the honors.

775
01:32:18.500 --> 01:32:19.667
Let's have lunch.

776
01:32:34.833 --> 01:32:35.833
Eugénie.

777
01:32:39.167 --> 01:32:43.000
Thank you. Suzanne.
this is Prince Andrea Cavalcanti.

778
01:32:43.083 --> 01:32:45.250
the Count of Monte Cristo's Italian protégé.

779
01:32:45.333 --> 01:32:46.458
He watches over me.

780
01:32:46.542 --> 01:32:49.042
My father fears Paris' beauties
might make me act foolishly.

781
01:32:49.833 --> 01:32:51.375
Your French is impeccable.

782
01:32:51.875 --> 01:32:56.000
That's because I had a strict teacher.
he beat my accent out of me.

783
01:32:56.875 --> 01:32:59.333
- That's terrible!
- I'm just kidding.

784
01:32:59.875 --> 01:33:02.625
- My mother's French.
- What an idiot.

785
01:33:03.125 --> 01:33:05.333
I'm so glad you could join us.

786
01:33:06.125 --> 01:33:10.417
Your protégé's hand didn't shake.
The animal didn't even suffer.

787
01:33:10.500 --> 01:33:12.708
And he's an expert on executions.

788
01:33:13.917 --> 01:33:15.708
Do you often carry out executions?

789
01:33:15.792 --> 01:33:18.167
Oh. much less than before. Count!

790
01:33:18.250 --> 01:33:21.375
- Forgiveness is in fashion.
- Dear friends. excuse the interruption.

791
01:33:21.458 --> 01:33:23.708
but I must introduce someone to the Count.

792
01:33:25.208 --> 01:33:26.375
- Count.
- Gentlemen.

793
01:33:46.542 --> 01:33:48.250
Yes. it's incredible.

794
01:33:49.333 --> 01:33:53.792
Darling. I'd like you to meet
the Count of Monte Cristo.

795
01:33:56.875 --> 01:33:58.250
Madame de Morcerf.

796
01:33:59.208 --> 01:34:00.250
It's a pleasure.

797
01:34:04.250 --> 01:34:05.542
Is everything all right. Mother?

798
01:34:07.083 --> 01:34:08.333
Yes. it's...

799
01:34:10.750 --> 01:34:14.292
I'm moved to meet the man
who has spared me from tears.

800
01:34:16.792 --> 01:34:18.958
Sir. I owe you my son's life.

801
01:34:20.292 --> 01:34:22.042
And for that. I bless you.

802
01:34:23.875 --> 01:34:27.167
Madam. you're rewarding me
too generously for a simple action.

803
01:34:28.375 --> 01:34:30.792
But I'm glad I saved you the grief.

804
01:34:31.750 --> 01:34:36.042
I've invited the Count to be our guest.
but he has always declined.

805
01:34:38.125 --> 01:34:40.208
Perhaps you'll have better luck than I did.

806
01:34:44.125 --> 01:34:47.250
Would you do me the pleasure
and honor of one day being our guest?

807
01:34:48.500 --> 01:34:49.792
Why. certainly. madam.

808
01:34:52.500 --> 01:34:55.667
Please excuse me.
I'd hate to take up any more of your time.

809
01:35:09.625 --> 01:35:10.875
What's the matter?

810
01:35:12.458 --> 01:35:15.417
- Do you want me to call someone?
- Albert.

811
01:35:16.542 --> 01:35:18.000
What do you know about him?

812
01:35:19.917 --> 01:35:20.958
Mother.

813
01:35:21.917 --> 01:35:24.625
I know you're always suspicious
of my new acquaintances.

814
01:35:25.125 --> 01:35:26.542
but the Count saved my life.

815
01:35:27.167 --> 01:35:28.500
He's as rich as a king.

816
01:35:29.500 --> 01:35:31.042
Why would I fear him?

817
01:35:34.542 --> 01:35:37.625
You're right. My fears are unfounded.

818
01:36:50.208 --> 01:36:53.500
Mr. King's Prosecutor. it is on my honor.

819
01:36:53.583 --> 01:36:56.708
as Lieutenant of the Royal Armies.
that I hereby attest

820
01:36:56.792 --> 01:37:00.083
that the man named Edmond Dantés
has testified in my presence

821
01:37:00.167 --> 01:37:04.417
and on numerous occasions to his sympathy
for the usurper and his desire

822
01:37:04.500 --> 01:37:07.208
to one day take up arms
to overthrow the monarchy.

823
01:37:08.042 --> 01:37:10.708
These words weigh heavily on me
for Edmond Dantes was my friend.

824
01:37:10.792 --> 01:37:13.375
but now I cannot let this crime go unpunished.

825
01:37:13.458 --> 01:37:16.417
I've seen too many men die
at the hands of traitors to the nation.

826
01:37:17.750 --> 01:37:19.542
That's not how you fall asleep. Count.

827
01:37:20.250 --> 01:37:21.750
I don't even want to sleep.

828
01:37:24.042 --> 01:37:25.583
Are you afraid of nightmares?

829
01:37:29.000 --> 01:37:30.958
I'm afraid I won't have them anymore.

830
01:37:32.250 --> 01:37:35.167
They help me keep my wounds open.

831
01:37:40.333 --> 01:37:41.667
Did you see her again?

832
01:37:43.042 --> 01:37:44.042
Yes.

833
01:37:47.500 --> 01:37:49.833
Was she as beautiful as you remember?

834
01:37:53.542 --> 01:37:55.875
I thought grief might have changed her.

835
01:37:59.500 --> 01:38:01.083
It must have been short-lived.

836
01:38:03.417 --> 01:38:05.833
Her eyes were not those
of a woman who had cried too much.

837
01:38:13.667 --> 01:38:16.792
She will become acquainted with tears
once we take her husband.

838
01:38:45.667 --> 01:38:46.667
I pass.

839
01:38:47.792 --> 01:38:50.625
I raise. 200 plus 500.

840
01:38:52.000 --> 01:38:53.208
I give up.

841
01:38:53.292 --> 01:38:56.208
I wouldn't invite you to my table
if you knew how to play.

842
01:38:57.750 --> 01:39:01.042
Voila. There are only three of us left. gentlemen.

843
01:39:03.208 --> 01:39:04.875
I'll leave you two alone.

844
01:39:10.125 --> 01:39:11.125
Two pairs.

845
01:39:12.417 --> 01:39:13.500
Bravo.

846
01:39:15.667 --> 01:39:16.750
Flush.

847
01:39:18.625 --> 01:39:22.542
You have too much heart for me. Baron.
I'm running away before I ruin my father.

848
01:39:22.625 --> 01:39:23.833
Come. Albert.

849
01:39:24.458 --> 01:39:26.750
Yes. that's it! Why don't you go see the ladies?

850
01:39:26.833 --> 01:39:28.917
Unlucky at cards. lucky in love!

851
01:39:32.875 --> 01:39:35.958
I'm fond of your prince. he's charming.

852
01:39:36.042 --> 01:39:39.958
I hardly know him. to be honest.
His father is a business acquaintance.

853
01:39:42.208 --> 01:39:44.000
A good family. no doubt.

854
01:39:44.500 --> 01:39:48.792
If by good you mean rich. then yes.
he's the second richest man in Italy.

855
01:39:50.458 --> 01:39:51.542
Second richest?

856
01:39:52.958 --> 01:39:54.833
You know the richest. I presume?

857
01:39:55.500 --> 01:39:57.250
Don't make me say something immodest.

858
01:39:58.458 --> 01:40:00.292
Finally. someone richer than me.

859
01:40:01.875 --> 01:40:04.917
His family dreams of him marrying a girl in Paris.

860
01:40:05.000 --> 01:40:08.208
but if the son is as fickle as the father. beware.

861
01:40:08.708 --> 01:40:09.833
Don't worry.

862
01:40:10.667 --> 01:40:12.958
I'm wary of everyone in general and...

863
01:40:13.792 --> 01:40:15.958
...especially of foreigners.

864
01:40:17.833 --> 01:40:19.542
I'm a foreigner myself.

865
01:40:19.625 --> 01:40:21.125
You don't count. Count.

866
01:40:21.750 --> 01:40:24.625
And you're a count. And it rhymes.

867
01:40:24.708 --> 01:40:26.000
You're a poet.

868
01:40:26.875 --> 01:40:30.708
Speaking of foreigners. the newspaper
The Independent was sold to an Englishman.

869
01:40:30.792 --> 01:40:34.875
Yes. a man named Halifax. a lord. I'm told.

870
01:40:36.667 --> 01:40:38.333
Lord Halifax only buys newspapers

871
01:40:38.417 --> 01:40:41.250
to spread fake news
and speculate on the stock market.

872
01:40:41.333 --> 01:40:43.000
He's a brigand of the worst kind.

873
01:40:44.333 --> 01:40:46.917
You don't seem to like this Lord very much--

874
01:40:47.000 --> 01:40:50.250
Well. let's just say I like a lot of people.

875
01:40:50.333 --> 01:40:53.125
but I only hate certain people.

876
01:40:53.208 --> 01:40:56.583
Well. hating an Englishman isn't a sin.
it's common sense.

877
01:41:00.750 --> 01:41:03.958
- Leaving so soon?
- It's almost midnight.

878
01:41:04.042 --> 01:41:05.875
Our carriage will turn into a pumpkin.

879
01:41:11.208 --> 01:41:12.208
Albert.

880
01:41:13.042 --> 01:41:15.792
Miss. you almost forgot your fan.

881
01:41:21.792 --> 01:41:22.917
Thank you. sir.

882
01:41:27.625 --> 01:41:28.750
I'm counting on you.

883
01:41:29.917 --> 01:41:30.958
For what?

884
01:41:31.542 --> 01:41:33.917
To join me in a dinner party
I'm hosting soon in Paris.

885
01:41:34.000 --> 01:41:35.792
I've finally got a place to stay.

886
01:41:37.667 --> 01:41:39.167
Of. of course.

887
01:41:40.375 --> 01:41:41.375
Good.

888
01:41:42.833 --> 01:41:43.833
See you soon.

889
01:41:51.417 --> 01:41:52.417
Count?

890
01:41:54.417 --> 01:41:55.625
Madame de Morcerf.

891
01:41:57.417 --> 01:42:00.333
- You're leaving as I arrive.
- Don't read anything into it.

892
01:42:02.083 --> 01:42:03.500
I just wanted to apologize.

893
01:42:06.000 --> 01:42:07.250
For what?

894
01:42:08.375 --> 01:42:09.875
For my dizziness the other day.

895
01:42:11.083 --> 01:42:14.292
You reminded me of someone
I knew well a long time ago

896
01:42:14.375 --> 01:42:16.625
who disappeared
under tragic circumstances.

897
01:42:20.750 --> 01:42:22.333
For a moment. I...

898
01:42:29.708 --> 01:42:32.250
See. it's happening again.
I'm at a loss for words.

899
01:42:34.792 --> 01:42:38.208
I'm the one who's sorry. ma'am.
for bringing up such a bad memory.

900
01:42:41.625 --> 01:42:43.167
Don't worry. it's gone now.

901
01:42:47.167 --> 01:42:48.167
I'm glad.

902
01:42:51.000 --> 01:42:52.458
I bid you good evening. madam.

903
01:42:53.917 --> 01:42:54.917
Count.

904
01:43:14.083 --> 01:43:15.125
It's from Albert.

905
01:43:22.667 --> 01:43:27.583
"Haydée. I'm not supposed to write to you.
That's why I'm not writing to you.

906
01:43:28.667 --> 01:43:30.125
I'm not supposed to meet you..."

907
01:43:30.958 --> 01:43:34.083
...that's why I'm not suggesting
that we meet in the Garden

908
01:43:34.167 --> 01:43:35.833
at 5:00 p.m. tomorrow.

909
01:43:36.375 --> 01:43:38.667
This place where I won't be tomorrow

910
01:43:38.750 --> 01:43:40.917
houses the most mysterious flowers in Paris.

911
01:43:42.333 --> 01:43:46.958
You're from a country we call
“the land of clouds and jasmine."

912
01:43:47.042 --> 01:43:51.458
We can trust Paris for the clouds.
I'll have jasmine in my boutonniere.

913
01:43:51.958 --> 01:43:53.875
So I won't say. "See you tomorrow.”

914
01:43:54.375 --> 01:43:56.958
And I won't tell you that ever since I saw you.

915
01:43:57.042 --> 01:43:59.875
I can't get your voice
or your face out of my head.

916
01:44:00.375 --> 01:44:01.542
Albert.

917
01:44:07.083 --> 01:44:10.250
- He's not going to report us?
- He's very loyal to the Count.

918
01:44:10.917 --> 01:44:12.833
But I think he likes me.

919
01:44:16.583 --> 01:44:17.833
It's a Strelitzia.

920
01:44:19.167 --> 01:44:22.083
Where I come from. there were some
on a path leading to the sea.

921
01:44:23.750 --> 01:44:25.667
It's also known as the bird of paradise.

922
01:44:26.542 --> 01:44:27.958
Bird of paradise.

923
01:44:28.708 --> 01:44:30.417
Bird of paradise?

924
01:44:31.417 --> 01:44:32.417
Good.

925
01:44:38.917 --> 01:44:41.125
How come you don't have a fiancée?

926
01:44:41.542 --> 01:44:43.458
Or perhaps you do.

927
01:44:44.750 --> 01:44:48.833
My father would like me
to marry a baron's daughter. but I...

928
01:44:49.750 --> 01:44:52.167
...I'm looking for something
this lady will never have.

929
01:44:53.208 --> 01:44:56.208
It's this indefinite charm

930
01:44:56.292 --> 01:44:59.375
that is to a woman
what perfume is to a flower.

931
01:45:00.000 --> 01:45:01.542
Or what flavor is to fruit.

932
01:45:03.125 --> 01:45:07.375
I don't know if Parisian girls
like to be picked or eaten. but I don't.

933
01:45:08.417 --> 01:45:11.042
- I'm sorry. I didn't mean it like that.
- I'm teasing you.

934
01:45:12.208 --> 01:45:14.292
Will you be at
the Count's dinner on Saturday?

935
01:45:14.958 --> 01:45:17.583
No. I'll be my mother's alibi.

936
01:45:17.667 --> 01:45:19.583
She shuns social gatherings like the plague.

937
01:45:20.292 --> 01:45:21.292
What about you?

938
01:45:22.625 --> 01:45:24.000
I don't know your mother.

939
01:45:24.958 --> 01:45:26.458
I don't know what she likes.

940
01:45:27.292 --> 01:45:28.875
but I share her dislikes.

941
01:45:33.542 --> 01:45:35.750
Neither he nor his mother
will be coming to dinner.

942
01:45:36.833 --> 01:45:39.083
But Fernand de Morcerf will be there.

943
01:45:46.625 --> 01:45:47.625
What's wrong?

944
01:45:49.625 --> 01:45:51.625
Aren't you gonna tell me about Albert?

945
01:45:54.458 --> 01:45:55.792
There is nothing to tell.

946
01:46:08.667 --> 01:46:10.042
It's normal to have doubts.

947
01:46:12.167 --> 01:46:14.417
To be afraid. I understand that.

948
01:46:16.667 --> 01:46:19.458
But when the time comes. you must remember--

949
01:46:19.542 --> 01:46:23.292
I don't need you to remind me
what his father did to mine.

950
01:46:31.167 --> 01:46:33.250
He couldn't help but put his lips on it.

951
01:46:55.625 --> 01:46:57.458
- Thank you.
- Watch your step.

952
01:47:01.042 --> 01:47:02.083
My dear friends.

953
01:47:10.333 --> 01:47:11.500
Good evening. Victoria.

954
01:47:15.750 --> 01:47:18.250
I was also expecting
something more spectacular.

955
01:47:18.333 --> 01:47:19.917
You don't have to make that face.

956
01:47:20.000 --> 01:47:23.208
Count on the Count to have
some surprises in store for us inside.

957
01:47:46.667 --> 01:47:49.500
You don't have much of an appetite.
Mr. de Villefort.

958
01:47:49.583 --> 01:47:51.917
Well. I had an appetite
before the pork and the fowl.

959
01:47:53.333 --> 01:47:54.500
This is...

960
01:47:55.917 --> 01:47:59.375
- ...a beautiful house.
- I sense you're surprised. Baron.

961
01:47:59.458 --> 01:48:00.958
Nothing gets past you. Count.

962
01:48:03.208 --> 01:48:07.000
To be honest. I thought a man like you
would choose a more central part of town.

963
01:48:07.083 --> 01:48:10.333
like the Champs-Elysées or St. Germain.

964
01:48:10.417 --> 01:48:14.083
Well. I bought this house
because I was advised not to.

965
01:48:14.792 --> 01:48:15.917
Why is that?

966
01:48:16.667 --> 01:48:19.167
Well. it's said to be haunted.

967
01:48:19.875 --> 01:48:24.125
They say a heinous crime
was committed here years ago.

968
01:48:24.208 --> 01:48:26.750
Beware. we have with us the King's Prosecutor.

969
01:48:26.833 --> 01:48:28.083
It's true.

970
01:48:29.167 --> 01:48:30.917
They say a child was sacrificed.

971
01:48:33.333 --> 01:48:37.000
- That's terrible!
- And you bought the house anyway.

972
01:48:37.083 --> 01:48:38.458
And you did the right thing.

973
01:48:39.083 --> 01:48:44.750
All these ridiculous ghost stories
are made up by malicious servants.

974
01:48:44.833 --> 01:48:47.958
- Or jealous neighbors.
- You're wrong. Prosecutor.

975
01:48:48.542 --> 01:48:50.667
I've lived in Asia and India.

976
01:48:51.500 --> 01:48:55.500
it's hard to return from these trips
without realizing that there's

977
01:48:55.583 --> 01:48:58.958
an invisible world populated by spirits.

978
01:49:00.542 --> 01:49:02.917
When I first visited this house. I...

979
01:49:04.000 --> 01:49:05.167
...I knew right away.

980
01:49:07.000 --> 01:49:11.708
I had a strange feeling that a crime
had indeed been committed here.

981
01:49:12.792 --> 01:49:15.208
So. I asked to be left alone for the night.

982
01:49:15.292 --> 01:49:17.042
But weren't you afraid?

983
01:49:18.542 --> 01:49:21.458
If your conscience is pure.
ghosts don't haunt you.

984
01:49:22.333 --> 01:49:24.958
- They speak to you.
- And what did they tell you?

985
01:49:25.042 --> 01:49:27.625
Yes. what did they say?

986
01:49:31.333 --> 01:49:37.375
That night. I settled down here.
right in front of this fireplace.

987
01:49:39.542 --> 01:49:42.583
I smoked some opium to be more receptive.

988
01:49:43.375 --> 01:49:46.625
There's nothing like it to broaden
the spectrum of your consciousness.

989
01:49:49.958 --> 01:49:51.792
In the sweetness of the smoke...

990
01:49:54.250 --> 01:49:57.083
...I felt like I was floating.

991
01:49:59.875 --> 01:50:01.708
I heard a bang in the wall.

992
01:50:03.417 --> 01:50:04.625
Followed by another.

993
01:50:08.375 --> 01:50:12.458
I laid my hand on the wall
and I heard screams coming from upstairs.

994
01:50:13.542 --> 01:50:18.917
I climbed the stairs.
The screams turned into groans.

995
01:50:20.958 --> 01:50:23.750
They were coming from a room
at the end of the hall.

996
01:50:26.167 --> 01:50:29.083
I opened the door and found myself in a room.

997
01:50:29.167 --> 01:50:32.375
In the middle. there was a bed.
I put my hand there.

998
01:50:35.708 --> 01:50:37.958
I saw a woman writhing in pain.

999
01:50:38.458 --> 01:50:43.083
She was given birth to a child.
She was alone. Abandoned.

1000
01:50:43.917 --> 01:50:44.917
Screaming.

1001
01:50:47.625 --> 01:50:50.208
And that's when I felt
a presence behind my back.

1002
01:50:51.333 --> 01:50:52.333
Suddenly...

1003
01:50:55.542 --> 01:50:57.167
You're scaring the ladies. Count.

1004
01:50:57.250 --> 01:50:58.333
And delighting us.

1005
01:50:58.958 --> 01:51:00.875
Go on. Count. I beseech you!

1006
01:51:00.958 --> 01:51:03.625
Pull yourself together. dear.
You're spoiling the fun.

1007
01:51:03.708 --> 01:51:06.333
I turned around. trembling.

1008
01:51:08.333 --> 01:51:12.500
And then I heard a whisper in my ear.

1009
01:51:14.500 --> 01:51:15.750
It was a child's voice.

1010
01:51:17.667 --> 01:51:20.667
A child's voice begging me to set him free.

1011
01:51:22.625 --> 01:51:27.250
I found a door.
A back door I hadn't seen in the dark.

1012
01:51:28.583 --> 01:51:31.833
I opened it. there were stairs.

1013
01:51:31.917 --> 01:51:33.042
They led to the garden.

1014
01:51:33.667 --> 01:51:36.875
And that's when I heard it again.
the child's voice.

1015
01:51:36.958 --> 01:51:39.542
He told me he'd been alone for so long.

1016
01:51:39.625 --> 01:51:42.667
He was crying.
He was crying out for his mother.

1017
01:51:48.042 --> 01:51:51.542
I searched all night. but...

1018
01:51:53.333 --> 01:51:54.875
...the garden was too big.

1019
01:51:56.917 --> 01:51:58.417
So. what did you do?

1020
01:52:08.042 --> 01:52:09.125
I'm sorry?

1021
01:52:10.542 --> 01:52:12.167
The garden was too big.

1022
01:52:13.042 --> 01:52:14.208
What did you do?

1023
01:52:16.375 --> 01:52:17.375
Oh. right.

1024
01:52:27.750 --> 01:52:31.500
Well. the next morning.
we started digging... everywhere.

1025
01:52:32.708 --> 01:52:37.458
We ripped out the apple trees.
dug up the trail. but nothing.

1026
01:52:40.333 --> 01:52:43.250
So. I brought a truffle pig from Périgord.

1027
01:52:45.333 --> 01:52:46.375
And?

1028
01:52:49.000 --> 01:52:50.833
Since he didn't find anything either...

1029
01:52:52.083 --> 01:52:53.708
...we ate him tonight.

1030
01:52:55.083 --> 01:52:56.083
Wonderful!

1031
01:52:57.792 --> 01:52:59.917
I told you it was all a fairy tale.

1032
01:53:01.208 --> 01:53:02.875
A fairy tale. Exactly.

1033
01:53:04.000 --> 01:53:07.167
Or so I thought... until yesterday.

1034
01:53:08.750 --> 01:53:12.083
As we were planting the torches
in the ground for tonight's reception.

1035
01:53:13.000 --> 01:53:15.208
one of them snapped in two.

1036
01:53:16.833 --> 01:53:18.750
So we dug around there and...

1037
01:53:20.333 --> 01:53:22.333
...we found a chest.

1038
01:53:22.417 --> 01:53:23.417
And?

1039
01:53:25.167 --> 01:53:26.500
What was in it?

1040
01:53:28.542 --> 01:53:31.167
- I don't know.
- What do you mean. you don't know?

1041
01:53:32.792 --> 01:53:35.375
Well. I waited for you to open it.

1042
01:53:53.000 --> 01:53:54.542
What if there's a body inside?

1043
01:53:56.250 --> 01:53:58.000
We'll give him a proper burial.

1044
01:54:03.167 --> 01:54:06.000
Prosecutor. perhaps you'd like to open it?

1045
01:54:10.042 --> 01:54:12.333
- I beg you. don't open it.
- Victoria. stop it!

1046
01:54:35.500 --> 01:54:36.958
Abracadabra.

1047
01:54:41.667 --> 01:54:44.333
I don't know how much of this is true.

1048
01:54:44.417 --> 01:54:46.583
but you are a magician. Count.

1049
01:54:52.667 --> 01:54:55.917
How is it possible? It's like he was there!

1050
01:54:56.458 --> 01:54:57.875
All those details were--

1051
01:54:58.375 --> 01:55:00.833
- I thought I'd go mad.
- Please. calm down.

1052
01:55:01.417 --> 01:55:03.375
- Where is our child's body?
- I don't know.

1053
01:55:03.875 --> 01:55:05.583
- You left it there. didn't you?
- Yes.

1054
01:55:06.208 --> 01:55:07.667
- You told me he was dead.
- Yes.

1055
01:55:07.750 --> 01:55:10.500
- You told me he was dead.
- Of course he was dead.

1056
01:55:10.583 --> 01:55:13.000
- Then where is he?
- I don't know. dear.

1057
01:55:13.083 --> 01:55:15.292
- Where is our child?
- I don't know!

1058
01:55:15.375 --> 01:55:18.458
Calm down. you're hysterical! I don't know.

1059
01:55:20.333 --> 01:55:21.333
Calm down.

1060
01:55:22.833 --> 01:55:24.167
I do know one thing.

1061
01:55:24.875 --> 01:55:28.833
Before a week goes by.
I'll find out who this Monte Cristo is.

1062
01:55:29.542 --> 01:55:32.125
Where he's from. where he's going.

1063
01:55:32.917 --> 01:55:35.917
and why he talks
about buried children in front of us.

1064
01:55:40.667 --> 01:55:44.500
Danglars is only suspicious of people
who are after his money.

1065
01:55:44.583 --> 01:55:47.750
Morcerf trusts me blindly
ever since I saved his son's life.

1066
01:55:48.250 --> 01:55:51.500
Only Villefort is left. Villefort is a prosecutor.

1067
01:55:51.583 --> 01:55:52.875
He's a wary man.

1068
01:55:53.750 --> 01:55:55.000
After this dinner.

1069
01:55:55.667 --> 01:55:57.708
Victoria will demand an explanation.

1070
01:55:57.792 --> 01:56:01.583
So. to reassure her and to reassure himself.
he will investigate.

1071
01:56:02.583 --> 01:56:06.042
And since we always learn so much more
from ill-intentioned mouths.

1072
01:56:06.125 --> 01:56:08.167
he'll go to the Count's sworn enemy.

1073
01:56:09.333 --> 01:56:10.583
Lord Halifax.

1074
01:56:12.083 --> 01:56:13.542
What do you want to know?

1075
01:56:13.625 --> 01:56:17.917
If there's anything I can do to hurt him.
it will be my pleasure.

1076
01:56:18.958 --> 01:56:22.208
Has the Count ever been to Paris?
He says he hasn't.

1077
01:56:22.292 --> 01:56:25.333
If he'd been here before. I'd know.

1078
01:56:25.958 --> 01:56:29.625
In that case. do you know
where he was 15 years ago?

1079
01:56:30.458 --> 01:56:32.458
Yes. in India.

1080
01:56:33.875 --> 01:56:36.042
But I must say...

1081
01:56:37.958 --> 01:56:40.542
...at the time. I still found him amusing.

1082
01:56:41.958 --> 01:56:43.625
But then...

1083
01:56:44.750 --> 01:56:45.750
Then what?

1084
01:56:46.833 --> 01:56:52.792
One night. I was correcting
a servant who had it coming.

1085
01:56:54.042 --> 01:56:59.542
But Monte Cristo had a passion
for those savages.

1086
01:56:59.625 --> 01:57:04.167
with their pagan god and their absurd magic.

1087
01:57:04.667 --> 01:57:07.042
Ridiculous beliefs. you know!

1088
01:57:08.333 --> 01:57:10.333
Then. he challenged me to a duel.

1089
01:57:11.792 --> 01:57:16.333
- For an indigenous person?
- Yes. an indigenous person.

1090
01:57:16.417 --> 01:57:18.000
Would you believe that?

1091
01:57:19.542 --> 01:57:23.125
Oh! It's hot. Aren't you hot? It's hot in here--

1092
01:57:23.208 --> 01:57:26.917
Can someone get me my fan.
for goodness' sake?

1093
01:57:27.000 --> 01:57:28.625
We're dying out here!

1094
01:57:30.583 --> 01:57:31.875
Not this--

1095
01:57:32.833 --> 01:57:33.958
Thank you.

1096
01:57:39.333 --> 01:57:42.125
And you. Mr. de Villefort?

1097
01:57:43.375 --> 01:57:45.583
- What did he do to you?
- Nothing.

1098
01:57:47.583 --> 01:57:50.750
I'm not sure yet if I should count him
as my friend or my enemy.

1099
01:57:51.750 --> 01:57:55.542
If he was your enemy. you would already know.

1100
01:57:55.625 --> 01:58:00.375
He's a lot of things.
but he's not one to hide his intentions.

1101
01:58:01.542 --> 01:58:06.000
But... be careful. Mr. Prosecutor.

1102
01:58:08.083 --> 01:58:13.667
If he becomes your friend.
that will make you my enemy.

1103
01:58:15.708 --> 01:58:16.750
Of course.

1104
01:58:24.833 --> 01:58:25.917
Yes!

1105
01:58:26.500 --> 01:58:28.583
Thank you. Mr. de Villefort.

1106
01:58:28.667 --> 01:58:32.250
It's been very nice chatting with you.
but I've got a lot of work to do.

1107
01:58:32.875 --> 01:58:34.417
Thank you. Lord Halifax.

1108
01:58:35.250 --> 01:58:36.875
Mr. Prosecutor.

1109
01:58:46.083 --> 01:58:47.083
Victor.

1110
01:58:48.958 --> 01:58:50.000
Yes. Count?

1111
01:58:50.083 --> 01:58:52.125
Get the horses ready.
we're going back to the castle.

1112
01:59:03.583 --> 01:59:05.667
Now that Villefort's guard is down.

1113
01:59:05.750 --> 01:59:07.875
we have plenty of time to prepare our attack.

1114
01:59:09.583 --> 01:59:12.833
I'm going south. I'll be back
for the party Danglars is organizing

1115
01:59:12.917 --> 01:59:14.458
for his daughter's 20th birthday.

1116
01:59:15.250 --> 01:59:18.458
During my journey. I'm counting on you.
André. to get closer to her.

1117
01:59:19.667 --> 01:59:22.792
And on you. Haydée. to bewitch Albert.

1118
01:59:30.208 --> 01:59:33.333
It can hold 600 slaves. 700 if you push a little.

1119
01:59:33.417 --> 01:59:35.458
But I'm a humanist.

1120
01:59:36.292 --> 01:59:37.792
I call it The Hercules.

1121
01:59:37.875 --> 01:59:40.750
My mom used to say all the time
that this is the line of people

1122
01:59:40.833 --> 01:59:42.083
who will do great things.

1123
01:59:43.167 --> 01:59:46.250
And this is your love line.

1124
01:59:47.667 --> 01:59:50.500
And here. I see that--

1125
01:59:50.583 --> 01:59:52.417
Andrea. I have to tell you something.

1126
01:59:59.375 --> 02:00:00.375
Yes?

1127
02:00:03.542 --> 02:00:06.500
I want to love you. but I can't.

1128
02:00:07.583 --> 02:00:08.667
I know.

1129
02:00:11.542 --> 02:00:14.750
I know you'll never be able to give me
that which you feel for Suzanne.

1130
02:00:14.833 --> 02:00:17.792
- It'll be our secret.
- Don't worry. it'll be our secret.

1131
02:00:17.875 --> 02:00:20.875
- I'll keep it well guarded.
- I know what it's like to play two roles.

1132
02:00:21.375 --> 02:00:23.208
I know what it's like to play two roles.

1133
02:00:25.125 --> 02:00:26.708
To not be able to be who you are.

1134
02:00:29.500 --> 02:00:30.667
I'll be your alibi.

1135
02:01:13.083 --> 02:01:15.250
It's time to redeem yourself.

1136
02:02:02.625 --> 02:02:06.000
I relive every second
of these moments with you in my dreams.

1137
02:02:07.000 --> 02:02:09.542
I'll take the memory of your eyes
with me into the night.

1138
02:02:10.833 --> 02:02:14.917
And I speak to no one because I don't want
to waste the echo of your words

1139
02:02:15.000 --> 02:02:16.542
that still tremble in my heart.

1140
02:02:18.208 --> 02:02:20.167
I keep your sheet music close to me.

1141
02:02:21.208 --> 02:02:23.583
I love it for how it makes me think of you.

1142
02:02:24.417 --> 02:02:27.750
but also. above all. I love it
for the memory it will bear forever.

1143
02:02:28.458 --> 02:02:31.542
That of a moment in life worth a lifetime.

1144
02:03:08.958 --> 02:03:10.458
- See you later.
- See you later.

1145
02:03:23.208 --> 02:03:24.208
Prince.

1146
02:03:28.208 --> 02:03:30.792
Eugénie. This party is just like you.

1147
02:03:30.875 --> 02:03:33.208
- lively and happy.
- Thank you. Andrea.

1148
02:03:33.792 --> 02:03:36.958
Will the Count of Monte Cristo
be among your guests this evening?

1149
02:03:37.750 --> 02:03:40.042
- Seventeen.
- Seventeen?

1150
02:03:40.750 --> 02:03:43.250
You're the 17th person to ask me that question.

1151
02:03:43.333 --> 02:03:45.583
And what have you told everybody?

1152
02:03:45.667 --> 02:03:47.542
There won't be an 18th.

1153
02:03:47.625 --> 02:03:48.667
There he is.

1154
02:03:53.667 --> 02:03:54.667
Excuse me.

1155
02:04:00.250 --> 02:04:02.000
Miss. Count.

1156
02:04:02.458 --> 02:04:04.750
- How was your trip?
- Splendid.

1157
02:04:05.625 --> 02:04:07.042
Thank you. Albert.

1158
02:04:07.125 --> 02:04:09.458
Eugénie is looking forward to seeing you. miss.

1159
02:04:10.375 --> 02:04:12.292
Count. may 1?

1160
02:04:12.917 --> 02:04:14.000
Of course.

1161
02:04:22.625 --> 02:04:24.583
Does the Count know we've been together?

1162
02:04:25.417 --> 02:04:26.625
I haven't told him.

1163
02:04:28.208 --> 02:04:29.875
Do you think he can figure it out?

1164
02:04:30.625 --> 02:04:32.208
God knows what he's capable of.

1165
02:04:33.792 --> 02:04:35.167
They're beautiful. aren't they?

1166
02:04:37.083 --> 02:04:38.792
They look so eager to live.

1167
02:04:40.542 --> 02:04:44.000
We're always in a hurry to be happy.
are we not?

1168
02:04:48.125 --> 02:04:50.042
Count. allow me the honor of your arm.

1169
02:04:50.792 --> 02:04:52.167
I feel like taking a walk.

1170
02:05:30.667 --> 02:05:31.875
Your hand is shaking.

1171
02:05:33.125 --> 02:05:34.208
You seem cold.

1172
02:05:35.333 --> 02:05:37.833
In my family.
we have cold hands. but warm hearts.

1173
02:05:39.083 --> 02:05:41.542
Here. this will warm us up.

1174
02:05:42.875 --> 02:05:47.583
Our grapes don't taste like your Sicily grapes.
but you'll be forgiving of our northern sun.

1175
02:05:48.250 --> 02:05:49.417
I apologize.

1176
02:05:51.875 --> 02:05:55.667
I apologize. madam. but... I never drink.

1177
02:05:58.708 --> 02:06:00.708
In that case. may I offer you something to eat?

1178
02:06:03.000 --> 02:06:04.750
I'm going to have to decline again.

1179
02:06:06.792 --> 02:06:07.875
Count.

1180
02:06:09.000 --> 02:06:10.125
There's an Arab custom

1181
02:06:10.208 --> 02:06:14.042
that creates eternal friendship for those
who share bread and salt under one roof.

1182
02:06:15.375 --> 02:06:16.625
I know that. madam.

1183
02:06:17.583 --> 02:06:19.667
But this is Paris. not Tangier.

1184
02:06:21.042 --> 02:06:25.083
In France. there are neither eternal friendships
nor the sharing of bread and salt.

1185
02:06:47.250 --> 02:06:50.125
But we are friends. aren't we?

1186
02:06:51.250 --> 02:06:52.292
Why. certainly.

1187
02:06:53.458 --> 02:06:54.750
Why wouldn't we?

1188
02:06:59.417 --> 02:07:01.042
Instead of bread and salt.

1189
02:07:01.125 --> 02:07:04.167
maybe you would like to share
some of your memories?

1190
02:07:06.792 --> 02:07:08.458
What do you wish to know. madam?

1191
02:07:11.333 --> 02:07:13.083
Is it true that you have seen much.

1192
02:07:13.958 --> 02:07:16.792
and traveled. and suffered?

1193
02:07:17.625 --> 02:07:19.042
What makes you say that?

1194
02:07:21.125 --> 02:07:22.125
Your eyes.

1195
02:07:25.083 --> 02:07:27.833
They say every great traveler
is searching for something

1196
02:07:27.917 --> 02:07:29.250
or running from something.

1197
02:07:31.583 --> 02:07:32.917
And have you found it?

1198
02:07:33.625 --> 02:07:35.000
I haven't finished my journey.

1199
02:07:40.625 --> 02:07:41.833
You live alone.

1200
02:07:44.125 --> 02:07:47.375
I have no sister. no son. no father.

1201
02:07:51.292 --> 02:07:55.500
I only have Haydée.
who I'm sure will leave me soon.

1202
02:07:58.708 --> 02:08:02.958
How can you live like this.
with nothing to hold on to?

1203
02:08:07.167 --> 02:08:08.667
I was in love with a young woman.

1204
02:08:11.917 --> 02:08:13.167
I was going to marry her.

1205
02:08:16.000 --> 02:08:17.125
Years ago.

1206
02:08:18.042 --> 02:08:21.542
But when the war came.
it took me away from her.

1207
02:08:26.000 --> 02:08:28.167
I thought she loved me enough to wait for me.

1208
02:08:33.208 --> 02:08:35.208
To remain faithful to me until the grave.

1209
02:08:39.125 --> 02:08:40.708
But when I came back...

1210
02:08:42.042 --> 02:08:43.250
...she was married.

1211
02:08:47.292 --> 02:08:50.875
Maybe my heart was more fragile...

1212
02:08:53.958 --> 02:08:56.083
...but I've endured more suffering.

1213
02:08:57.417 --> 02:09:00.208
- That's my story.
- And that love stayed with you?

1214
02:09:03.875 --> 02:09:05.250
You only really love once.

1215
02:09:06.958 --> 02:09:08.042
Right?

1216
02:09:10.625 --> 02:09:12.250
Did you ever see this woman again?

1217
02:09:16.667 --> 02:09:17.667
Never.

1218
02:09:18.792 --> 02:09:19.917
Never?

1219
02:09:24.500 --> 02:09:25.500
Never.

1220
02:09:32.542 --> 02:09:34.875
Did you ever forgive her
for what she did to you?

1221
02:09:37.792 --> 02:09:40.250
We can only forgive those
who ask for our forgiveness.

1222
02:09:45.417 --> 02:09:47.333
What if she asked for it today?

1223
02:10:05.167 --> 02:10:08.917
Buy The Independent!
Danglars' fleet stolen from Marseille!

1224
02:10:09.000 --> 02:10:13.125
Buy The Independent. ladies and gentlemen.
The Independent!

1225
02:10:13.792 --> 02:10:17.375
How can someone steal boats
from a harbor in broad daylight?

1226
02:10:17.458 --> 02:10:20.125
- Were they insured?
- What do you think?

1227
02:10:20.583 --> 02:10:22.958
Danglars' stock is plummeting
in the stock market.

1228
02:10:24.125 --> 02:10:25.792
But thanks to the Army telegraph.

1229
02:10:26.500 --> 02:10:31.250
Danglars will learn before anybody else
that nothing happened in Marseille.

1230
02:10:31.542 --> 02:10:33.708
Weren't you supposed to steal those boats?

1231
02:10:33.792 --> 02:10:36.250
- Good things come to those who wait.
- You're saved.

1232
02:10:37.042 --> 02:10:38.625
Your boats are still there.

1233
02:10:38.708 --> 02:10:40.292
- What?
- The Independent lied.

1234
02:10:42.500 --> 02:10:47.958
"Danglars" fleet
is still docked at Marseille Harbor."

1235
02:10:50.333 --> 02:10:52.833
Thank you! Thank you. friends!

1236
02:10:52.917 --> 02:10:56.083
Danglars will remember
what I told him. and he'll think--

1237
02:10:56.167 --> 02:11:00.750
That's a move from the new boss
of The Independent. our dear Lord Halifax.

1238
02:11:00.833 --> 02:11:01.875
That's right.

1239
02:11:02.708 --> 02:11:04.208
Monte Cristo was right.

1240
02:11:04.292 --> 02:11:07.250
That English pig is using his newspaper
to speculate about me.

1241
02:11:07.333 --> 02:11:09.000
We must issue a denial.

1242
02:11:11.167 --> 02:11:14.542
- Absolutely not.
- I don't understand. You have to--

1243
02:11:16.542 --> 02:11:17.583
Do you hear that?

1244
02:11:18.917 --> 02:11:19.917
Listen.

1245
02:11:21.000 --> 02:11:22.083
What a lovely sound.

1246
02:11:24.250 --> 02:11:25.500
A lovely little sound.

1247
02:11:27.417 --> 02:11:29.375
The sound of money falling.

1248
02:11:30.167 --> 02:11:32.542
- I don't understand.
- Think.

1249
02:11:33.083 --> 02:11:35.500
He knows something no one else knows yet.

1250
02:11:36.208 --> 02:11:40.125
Imagine you're playing poker
and you know your opponent's hand.

1251
02:11:40.875 --> 02:11:43.083
- What do you do?
- I raise.

1252
02:11:43.167 --> 02:11:44.583
The stocks are at an all-time low.

1253
02:11:45.708 --> 02:11:49.917
If I buy them. in two days
I'll have made an extraordinary profit.

1254
02:11:50.625 --> 02:11:51.958
My finest move.

1255
02:11:52.042 --> 02:11:54.958
Buy back your shares?
How much would it cost?

1256
02:11:55.042 --> 02:11:57.417
- Five hundred million! Yes.
- Five hundred million?

1257
02:11:58.250 --> 02:11:59.542
But it has to be done today.

1258
02:12:00.042 --> 02:12:03.750
Before the market closes.
and before that bastard Halifax does it.

1259
02:12:04.500 --> 02:12:06.875
How are you going
to get 500 million by tonight?

1260
02:12:09.458 --> 02:12:12.292
By going to Lord Halifax's greatest enemy.

1261
02:12:40.792 --> 02:12:42.458
I'm sorry. Baron. but...

1262
02:12:43.458 --> 02:12:45.708
...the sea has always brought me bad luck.

1263
02:12:45.792 --> 02:12:48.292
- I won't buy back your shares.
- Count--

1264
02:12:49.167 --> 02:12:53.042
However. I never refuse to help
a friend and punish an enemy.

1265
02:12:53.125 --> 02:12:56.708
So I'll lend you the money.
and you can do whatever you want with it.

1266
02:12:59.958 --> 02:13:03.458
I can guarantee you a 20% interest rate.

1267
02:13:03.958 --> 02:13:06.125
No. I'll lend you the money interest-free.

1268
02:13:08.125 --> 02:13:11.333
There's a saying in Sicily.
"You don't get rich off a friend."

1269
02:13:11.417 --> 02:13:12.417
I insist.

1270
02:13:13.292 --> 02:13:17.250
I've had a mortgage drawn up
on my entire estate.

1271
02:13:17.333 --> 02:13:22.083
It's not 500 million. just 200 million.

1272
02:13:22.167 --> 02:13:25.583
- I can promise you that.
- Your word is good enough for me.

1273
02:13:25.667 --> 02:13:29.417
You know. in France. we say.
"Good accounts make good friends."

1274
02:13:31.500 --> 02:13:35.375
So be it. Then. as a friend.
I accept your personal guarantee.

1275
02:13:38.083 --> 02:13:40.167
In a week. I'll pay you back.

1276
02:13:42.417 --> 02:13:44.792
We're going to bring this Halifax to his knees.

1277
02:13:45.917 --> 02:13:47.125
A complaint is ready.

1278
02:13:47.958 --> 02:13:51.667
I'll take care of the claim myself.

1279
02:13:51.750 --> 02:13:55.458
Well. I'm looking forward to being
in court to witness this execution.

1280
02:14:17.292 --> 02:14:20.542
Lord Halifax. owner of The Independent.

1281
02:14:20.625 --> 02:14:22.708
who was called to the stand today

1282
02:14:22.792 --> 02:14:28.000
to answer defamation charges.
had to leave the country in a hurry.

1283
02:14:29.667 --> 02:14:34.375
But he pledges to have his representative
present at this court at 2:00.

1284
02:15:01.250 --> 02:15:04.167
Your Honor. the charade
has gone on long enough.

1285
02:15:04.250 --> 02:15:05.750
We are not here to play games.

1286
02:15:07.333 --> 02:15:11.292
I request Mr. Halifax's representative
to come forward if he is present.

1287
02:15:19.750 --> 02:15:22.250
What are you doing? It's not over yet.

1288
02:15:39.583 --> 02:15:41.375
I'm Lord Halifax's representative.

1289
02:15:45.792 --> 02:15:49.042
I stand before you because
The Independent has been accused

1290
02:15:49.125 --> 02:15:50.750
of spreading fake news.

1291
02:15:51.750 --> 02:15:53.167
I stand before you today...

1292
02:15:53.792 --> 02:15:56.417
...to say that Danglars' fleet is. in fact. gone.

1293
02:15:56.500 --> 02:15:58.875
Nonsense! My entire fleet is in Marseille!

1294
02:15:58.958 --> 02:16:00.500
Your Honor. this is a farce.

1295
02:16:02.333 --> 02:16:03.625
What proof do you have?

1296
02:16:04.042 --> 02:16:07.792
You must simply contact
the harbormaster of Marseille. Your Honor.

1297
02:16:07.875 --> 02:16:11.042
Then. you persist in your assertions?

1298
02:16:11.958 --> 02:16:15.458
I persist and sign. Your Honor.

1299
02:16:16.500 --> 02:16:18.792
But I would like to do so under my real name.

1300
02:16:18.875 --> 02:16:20.292
You have a fake one?

1301
02:16:24.000 --> 02:16:26.750
Everyone knows me as Andrea Cavalcanti.

1302
02:16:27.125 --> 02:16:28.917
After years on the streets.

1303
02:16:29.000 --> 02:16:33.167
I was taken in by a distinguished
and wealthy noble Italian family.

1304
02:16:33.875 --> 02:16:37.208
I grew up as a thief and ended up as a prince.

1305
02:16:37.833 --> 02:16:41.958
My new job isn't more honest than my last.
but it's much more enjoyable.

1306
02:16:45.250 --> 02:16:49.583
It was here in Paris that I was
finally able to trace my real father.

1307
02:16:55.750 --> 02:16:58.917
I was born on November 3rd. 1815.

1308
02:17:01.667 --> 02:17:02.708
In Auteuil.

1309
02:17:09.042 --> 02:17:10.500
Your Honor. can...

1310
02:17:11.958 --> 02:17:16.000
...the defendant...
present evidence to support his claim?

1311
02:17:16.083 --> 02:17:17.583
I'm coming to that. Mr. Prosecutor.

1312
02:17:18.875 --> 02:17:21.083
Believe me. your patience will be rewarded.

1313
02:17:24.708 --> 02:17:28.375
I am the bastard son
of a French aristocrat and his mistress!

1314
02:17:33.167 --> 02:17:39.125
My mother doesn't know I'm alive.
since my father told her I died at birth.

1315
02:17:41.250 --> 02:17:43.542
He wrapped me in cloth and buried me alive.

1316
02:17:46.208 --> 02:17:49.625
You speak. sir. of attempted infanticide.

1317
02:17:51.083 --> 02:17:52.542
It would've been the case...

1318
02:17:53.583 --> 02:17:56.500
...if my aunt hadn't heard my cries
and dug me out of the ground.

1319
02:17:56.583 --> 02:17:58.167
Who are you accusing?

1320
02:17:59.250 --> 02:18:00.583
A respectable man

1321
02:18:01.583 --> 02:18:02.750
that you all know.

1322
02:18:08.875 --> 02:18:10.500
His coat of arms is on this linen.

1323
02:18:15.833 --> 02:18:20.125
My father. the man who tried to kill me.
is none other than the man before me.

1324
02:18:24.375 --> 02:18:26.042
Prosecutor Villefort.

1325
02:18:31.625 --> 02:18:33.875
Quiet or I'll clear the court!

1326
02:18:33.958 --> 02:18:35.125
This is slander!

1327
02:18:36.458 --> 02:18:38.875
- I'll sue you!
- Mr. Cavalcanti.

1328
02:18:40.417 --> 02:18:42.750
Are you aware
of the magnitude of your accusations?

1329
02:18:42.833 --> 02:18:45.750
I warn you. I won't settle for a cloth.
even with blood on it.

1330
02:18:46.958 --> 02:18:49.708
The prosecutor will bring you
the proof of my claim himself.

1331
02:18:52.542 --> 02:18:54.042
- You're delirious.
- Father.

1332
02:18:56.917 --> 02:18:58.667
Please. don't make my mother testify.

1333
02:18:59.417 --> 02:19:01.333
She's been through enough already.

1334
02:19:12.833 --> 02:19:15.875
The trial is on hold until further investigation.

1335
02:19:15.958 --> 02:19:17.250
Everyone. leave the room!

1336
02:19:19.125 --> 02:19:20.125
One down.

1337
02:19:22.542 --> 02:19:27.042
Come on. Victoria. let's go!
Sorry! Let us through.

1338
02:19:39.167 --> 02:19:40.917
Why didn't you tell me the truth?

1339
02:19:42.333 --> 02:19:45.375
Your father wanted me
to be his son-in-law but...

1340
02:19:46.583 --> 02:19:48.875
...it's impossible because
we have the same mother.

1341
02:19:52.375 --> 02:19:55.625
Don't forget your lifeline. Be happy. Sister.

1342
02:20:11.958 --> 02:20:14.875
Count. Count!

1343
02:20:16.792 --> 02:20:20.167
This story doesn't make any sense.
It's complete madness.

1344
02:20:20.250 --> 02:20:23.500
My boats were still in Marseille yesterday. I--

1345
02:20:24.167 --> 02:20:27.667
I'm going to need
a little more time to pay you back.

1346
02:20:31.583 --> 02:20:33.083
You have nothing left. Baron.

1347
02:20:33.958 --> 02:20:35.958
Everything that was yours is now mine.

1348
02:20:37.042 --> 02:20:40.167
All you have left are the clothes on your back.

1349
02:20:42.083 --> 02:20:46.792
Leave Paris at once and maybe
I won't let your wife and daughter starve.

1350
02:20:47.875 --> 02:20:49.125
Come on. Count.

1351
02:20:49.208 --> 02:20:51.333
You think I'm harsh. Baron?

1352
02:20:54.667 --> 02:20:56.083
I know I am.

1353
02:20:57.958 --> 02:20:59.208
I take pride in that.

1354
02:21:13.000 --> 02:21:15.125
You should take your wife home.

1355
02:21:15.917 --> 02:21:17.000
She looks quite pale.

1356
02:21:26.458 --> 02:21:27.458
Two down.

1357
02:22:10.958 --> 02:22:12.000
Father!

1358
02:22:25.333 --> 02:22:26.583
A gift from Angéle!

1359
02:22:51.542 --> 02:22:53.750
- Out of the way!
- No!

1360
02:23:11.458 --> 02:23:12.625
Why. André?

1361
02:23:14.458 --> 02:23:15.500
Why?

1362
02:23:25.708 --> 02:23:26.750
Don't cry.

1363
02:24:46.125 --> 02:24:47.833
I knew it would end like this.

1364
02:24:49.333 --> 02:24:51.167
- I knew it.
- Haydée.

1365
02:24:56.042 --> 02:24:57.167
He didn't listen.

1366
02:24:59.667 --> 02:25:01.167
He didn't listen?

1367
02:25:06.208 --> 02:25:07.458
What didn't he listen to?

1368
02:25:10.875 --> 02:25:12.417
You taught him nothing but hate.

1369
02:25:13.375 --> 02:25:15.500
You're the one who put that dagger in his hand.

1370
02:25:19.167 --> 02:25:21.000
Only your grief speaks?

1371
02:25:24.333 --> 02:25:25.833
I loved him like a son.

1372
02:25:32.792 --> 02:25:33.917
Do you love me too?

1373
02:25:38.500 --> 02:25:41.250
Are you also willing
to sacrifice me for your revenge?

1374
02:25:43.042 --> 02:25:44.333
It's not revenge.

1375
02:25:46.083 --> 02:25:47.375
It's justice.

1376
02:25:53.750 --> 02:25:55.208
Remember your tears. Haydée!

1377
02:25:56.042 --> 02:25:58.875
Your mother's screams and your father's blood.

1378
02:25:58.958 --> 02:26:01.000
Do not forget the name
of the one who betrayed them.

1379
02:26:01.542 --> 02:26:02.875
Remember his name!

1380
02:26:34.667 --> 02:26:38.208
“If you love me as I love you.
don't ever come looking for me.

1381
02:26:38.750 --> 02:26:41.333
You're too noble-hearted to not understand me.

1382
02:26:41.417 --> 02:26:44.625
I save my strength to fight
against myself and drink my tears.

1383
02:26:45.167 --> 02:26:48.292
Be happy far from me. You deserve it."

1384
02:26:56.917 --> 02:26:57.958
Albert?

1385
02:27:35.500 --> 02:27:36.583
Albert.

1386
02:27:37.917 --> 02:27:40.500
Are you mad? You can't stay here.

1387
02:27:40.583 --> 02:27:43.292
Haydée. I've only known you a few months--

1388
02:27:43.375 --> 02:27:44.375
Leave.

1389
02:27:45.042 --> 02:27:46.833
Run from me like you run from the plague.

1390
02:27:48.333 --> 02:27:50.458
- I'll make you miserable.
- Run away with me.

1391
02:27:51.708 --> 02:27:52.917
I swear to you. Haydée.

1392
02:27:53.875 --> 02:27:56.500
I promise you happiness. not despair.

1393
02:27:58.333 --> 02:27:59.583
You don't know me.

1394
02:28:00.750 --> 02:28:02.417
You don't know the Count.

1395
02:28:02.500 --> 02:28:04.417
- Haydée--
- If you love me as I love you...

1396
02:28:08.208 --> 02:28:09.333
...say goodbye.

1397
02:28:11.208 --> 02:28:12.375
I beg you.

1398
02:28:15.542 --> 02:28:16.667
Say it!

1399
02:28:22.208 --> 02:28:23.500
I'll say it.

1400
02:28:25.500 --> 02:28:27.875
I vow before God. from the depths of my heart.

1401
02:28:31.292 --> 02:28:35.083
I wish you a life happy enough
to leave no room for memories of me.

1402
02:28:37.792 --> 02:28:39.042
Goodbye. my love.

1403
02:28:41.083 --> 02:28:42.458
Those. those eyes--

1404
02:28:46.042 --> 02:28:49.542
Without you. my life is meaningless.
My despair is guaranteed.

1405
02:28:51.000 --> 02:28:52.083
What are you going to do?

1406
02:28:53.875 --> 02:28:56.208
Don't worry. I'll keep my promise.

1407
02:28:57.083 --> 02:28:59.042
But for heaven's sake. you'll live. won't you?

1408
02:29:00.000 --> 02:29:01.083
What do you care?

1409
02:29:03.750 --> 02:29:05.417
Since I'm already dead to you.

1410
02:29:14.167 --> 02:29:15.250
Let's elope.

1411
02:29:28.833 --> 02:29:32.292
Haydée. If you wish to join the Morcerf family...

1412
02:29:33.250 --> 02:29:35.750
...I think Albert deserves to know your story.

1413
02:29:37.083 --> 02:29:41.500
If you remain silent.
I shall be forced to refuse or speak for you.

1414
02:29:43.208 --> 02:29:45.792
Do I really need to speak for you?

1415
02:29:46.667 --> 02:29:48.250
Count. please!

1416
02:29:48.792 --> 02:29:51.042
- Haydée is the daughter of--
- Stop!

1417
02:29:56.250 --> 02:29:57.417
I'll tell him myself.

1418
02:30:16.167 --> 02:30:17.708
My father was a famous man...

1419
02:30:18.750 --> 02:30:20.500
...known as Ali Tepelini.

1420
02:30:23.667 --> 02:30:24.958
Pasha of Yanina.

1421
02:30:32.542 --> 02:30:33.708
I was ten years old...

1422
02:30:34.500 --> 02:30:36.667
...when he was killed
in front of me and my mother.

1423
02:30:38.125 --> 02:30:40.000
He had welcomed a French soldier...

1424
02:30:41.042 --> 02:30:42.292
...who was our ally.

1425
02:30:44.667 --> 02:30:46.042
Shot by a dozen bullets...

1426
02:30:48.500 --> 02:30:51.542
...my father found
the strength to stand up.

1427
02:30:53.542 --> 02:30:55.750
And he shot the man who betrayed him.

1428
02:30:58.542 --> 02:30:59.875
He took out one of his eyes.

1429
02:31:03.042 --> 02:31:04.625
I never saw my mother again.

1430
02:31:07.708 --> 02:31:11.500
That officer sold me as a slave
to a Viach tribe from the Balkans.

1431
02:31:13.042 --> 02:31:14.250
- His name was--
- Enough.

1432
02:31:14.792 --> 02:31:15.875
Albert...

1433
02:31:21.250 --> 02:31:24.167
- You manipulated me from the beginning.
- I warned you.

1434
02:31:24.250 --> 02:31:27.667
- You used me.
- Don't say words you can't take back.

1435
02:31:27.750 --> 02:31:30.875
- Do you think I'm afraid of you?
- For the last time. stop provoking me.

1436
02:31:30.958 --> 02:31:34.917
- Albert. please-- Count!
- You've taken everything from me.

1437
02:31:35.667 --> 02:31:38.750
All I have left is my name.
and you've tarnished it.

1438
02:31:38.833 --> 02:31:39.833
No!

1439
02:31:40.750 --> 02:31:41.958
Count. I beg you!

1440
02:31:43.000 --> 02:31:45.250
Sir. I'll take your glove.

1441
02:31:45.333 --> 02:31:48.000
I'll give it back first thing
in the morning. with a bullet.

1442
02:31:56.500 --> 02:32:00.125
- Have you no mercy?
- Did they show mercy for Edmond Dantés?

1443
02:32:01.875 --> 02:32:03.083
Look at me.

1444
02:32:03.167 --> 02:32:07.125
I am nothing more than the agent
of fate's deaf and blind will.

1445
02:32:12.375 --> 02:32:15.000
And Fernand de Morcerf
will know what my father knew.

1446
02:32:18.500 --> 02:32:20.000
If you kill Albert...

1447
02:32:21.083 --> 02:32:24.125
...you won't be able to say. "God is mine.

1448
02:32:25.083 --> 02:32:26.458
God is with me."

1449
02:32:27.875 --> 02:32:29.417
You'll be a murderer.

1450
02:32:33.417 --> 02:32:37.417
It is written in the Bible that the sons
will pay for the crimes of their fathers.

1451
02:32:44.500 --> 02:32:46.167
Jacopo. follow her.

1452
02:33:26.958 --> 02:33:28.083
Jacopo. leave us.

1453
02:33:30.542 --> 02:33:31.542
Madam...

1454
02:33:32.458 --> 02:33:33.667
...what are you doing here?

1455
02:33:34.792 --> 02:33:36.458
Edmond. you won't kill my son.

1456
02:33:38.167 --> 02:33:39.625
What name did you say?

1457
02:33:40.292 --> 02:33:41.375
Yours.

1458
02:33:43.000 --> 02:33:45.917
Edmond. it's not Mrs. de Morcerf
in front of you. it's Mercedes.

1459
02:33:46.500 --> 02:33:48.083
I don't know anyone by that name.

1460
02:33:51.375 --> 02:33:53.292
I recognized you the second I saw you.

1461
02:33:54.375 --> 02:33:56.917
and even if I hadn't.
I'd have recognized your voice.

1462
02:33:57.000 --> 02:33:59.000
My mind refused to believe. but my heart knew.

1463
02:33:59.083 --> 02:34:03.167
I've been watching you since that day.
trying to figure out your plan for Morcerf.

1464
02:34:03.250 --> 02:34:05.250
You mean Fernand. madam.

1465
02:34:06.125 --> 02:34:08.667
Since we remember each other's names.
let's remember them all.

1466
02:34:12.000 --> 02:34:13.375
I'm the guilty one.

1467
02:34:15.292 --> 02:34:18.375
I'm the one who lacked strength
in the face of your absence.

1468
02:34:19.125 --> 02:34:22.542
I'm the one who didn't have faith
when I heard you were dead. Me!

1469
02:34:23.125 --> 02:34:25.667
Why? Why were you alone?

1470
02:34:26.458 --> 02:34:29.333
Why wasn't I here? Why was I arrested?

1471
02:34:29.833 --> 02:34:33.250
- Why was I given a death sentence? Why?
- I don't know.

1472
02:34:37.583 --> 02:34:39.917
I don't think he still writes you love letters.

1473
02:34:40.833 --> 02:34:43.292
But I think you'll easily
recognize his handwriting.

1474
02:34:46.542 --> 02:34:47.542
Take a look.

1475
02:34:48.792 --> 02:34:50.042
Look. Mercédés.

1476
02:34:52.667 --> 02:34:56.208
This is what your husband wrote
to Villefort 20 years ago.

1477
02:35:00.208 --> 02:35:02.125
I must avenge myself. Mercédés.

1478
02:35:03.792 --> 02:35:04.792
I must.

1479
02:35:06.833 --> 02:35:08.292
Then avenge yourself. Edmond.

1480
02:35:11.417 --> 02:35:12.875
But take revenge on the guilty.

1481
02:35:14.958 --> 02:35:16.750
On Fernand. who betrayed you.

1482
02:35:17.417 --> 02:35:19.500
Take revenge on me. but spare Albert.

1483
02:35:23.708 --> 02:35:25.583
If only you knew all the prayers...

1484
02:35:29.500 --> 02:35:31.667
...if only you knew the tears I've shed.

1485
02:35:32.667 --> 02:35:34.833
Did you lose your father in loneliness?

1486
02:35:35.333 --> 02:35:38.708
Did you see the one you loved
in the arms of your rival?

1487
02:35:40.500 --> 02:35:41.542
Did you?

1488
02:35:42.583 --> 02:35:43.583
No.

1489
02:35:44.417 --> 02:35:45.417
No.

1490
02:35:47.083 --> 02:35:49.167
But I see the man I never stopped loving...

1491
02:35:50.208 --> 02:35:52.000
...getting ready to murder my son.

1492
02:36:07.208 --> 02:36:08.542
What do you want. Mercédés?

1493
02:36:12.083 --> 02:36:13.458
Do you want your son to live?

1494
02:36:15.208 --> 02:36:16.208
He will.

1495
02:36:20.250 --> 02:36:21.292
Thank you.

1496
02:36:23.083 --> 02:36:24.333
Thank you. Edmond.

1497
02:36:30.042 --> 02:36:31.375
That's the man I know.

1498
02:36:33.417 --> 02:36:35.042
As I've always dreamed of you.

1499
02:36:36.125 --> 02:36:37.625
As I've always loved you.

1500
02:36:55.292 --> 02:36:56.917
But now it's time to say goodbye.

1501
02:36:59.083 --> 02:37:00.083
Goodbye?

1502
02:37:02.792 --> 02:37:04.542
If I give up on my revenge.

1503
02:37:05.750 --> 02:37:08.042
I give up on the only thing
that's keeping me alive.

1504
02:37:11.875 --> 02:37:13.375
The duel is tomorrow.

1505
02:37:16.417 --> 02:37:17.625
Goodbye. Mercédés.

1506
02:37:29.500 --> 02:37:30.958
Mr. Albert de Morcerf.

1507
02:37:31.625 --> 02:37:34.208
you have publicly provoked
the Count of Monte Cristo.

1508
02:37:35.458 --> 02:37:37.875
The duel will take place
at 20 paces on my command.

1509
02:37:39.292 --> 02:37:40.667
The insulted party goes first.

1510
02:37:46.417 --> 02:37:47.458
Take your positions.

1511
02:37:50.000 --> 02:37:51.000
Go on. gentlemen.

1512
02:38:14.458 --> 02:38:15.458
Fire!

1513
02:38:42.500 --> 02:38:43.500
Fire!

1514
02:39:27.542 --> 02:39:30.792
Do I detect a glimmer
of disappointment in your eyes?

1515
02:39:33.083 --> 02:39:36.417
I will never forgive you for taking his life.

1516
02:39:37.750 --> 02:39:39.333
And for breaking my heart.

1517
02:39:42.083 --> 02:39:43.167
So you did love him.

1518
02:39:44.750 --> 02:39:45.833
If I loved him?

1519
02:39:48.083 --> 02:39:51.250
Everything pushed me to hate him.
but who can explain why we fall in love?

1520
02:39:52.042 --> 02:39:55.458
No matter how hard we try
to reason with ourselves. it's too late.

1521
02:39:56.208 --> 02:39:57.542
We've lost our balance.

1522
02:40:00.500 --> 02:40:03.083
Our inner voice whispers
that there are no coincidences.

1523
02:40:04.083 --> 02:40:07.458
And instead of listening to that voice.
I listened to yours!

1524
02:40:10.292 --> 02:40:12.167
I would have made his misery and mine!

1525
02:40:14.958 --> 02:40:18.333
What am I going to do
with all this love I haven't given him?

1526
02:40:20.292 --> 02:40:22.667
These words I haven't told him?

1527
02:40:25.708 --> 02:40:26.958
You have told him.

1528
02:40:29.542 --> 02:40:30.667
He heard them.

1529
02:40:38.500 --> 02:40:39.542
Albert.

1530
02:40:55.208 --> 02:40:56.208
Count!

1531
02:41:03.875 --> 02:41:04.917
Run now.

1532
02:41:06.083 --> 02:41:08.375
Run and don't let anyone steal your happiness.

1533
02:41:48.708 --> 02:41:49.750
Edmond!

1534
02:41:56.083 --> 02:41:57.167
Edmond!

1535
02:42:02.625 --> 02:42:04.125
Show yourself. Edmond!

1536
02:42:10.333 --> 02:42:11.625
I've been waiting for you.

1537
02:42:12.833 --> 02:42:14.750
You're finally showing your true colors.

1538
02:42:15.750 --> 02:42:18.083
And I've been seeking
to uncover yours. Fernand.

1539
02:42:19.708 --> 02:42:21.458
To know who you really are.

1540
02:42:22.625 --> 02:42:24.250
So I followed in your footsteps.

1541
02:42:25.083 --> 02:42:26.750
I've been everywhere you've been.

1542
02:42:28.917 --> 02:42:30.458
I've met them all.

1543
02:42:31.417 --> 02:42:34.458
Your friends. your comrades in arms.
your enemies. all of them.

1544
02:42:36.167 --> 02:42:37.833
Who didn't you betray. Fernand?

1545
02:42:39.083 --> 02:42:40.750
To whom have you remained loyal?

1546
02:42:41.583 --> 02:42:43.625
Everywhere you've shown your true colors.

1547
02:42:45.125 --> 02:42:48.875
I lost faith in man... the day you betrayed me.

1548
02:42:51.500 --> 02:42:52.750
You should have killed me.

1549
02:42:53.333 --> 02:42:54.750
It's never too late.

1550
02:46:54.458 --> 02:46:55.458
Get up.

1551
02:47:16.750 --> 02:47:19.750
Look at me. Look at me!

1552
02:47:23.083 --> 02:47:24.125
Kill me.

1553
02:47:26.792 --> 02:47:28.667
We see greatness in those who are gone...

1554
02:47:30.125 --> 02:47:31.625
...and eventually we forgive them.

1555
02:47:37.750 --> 02:47:39.208
I don't want you to be forgiven.

1556
02:48:52.333 --> 02:48:53.417
<i>Mercédés.</i>

1557
02:48:54.083 --> 02:48:56.167
I've come to say goodbye where life

1558
02:48:56.250 --> 02:48:59.375
took us away from each other
21 years ago today.

1559
02:49:00.417 --> 02:49:04.000
So many things were broken
in me and around me since then

1560
02:49:04.083 --> 02:49:05.792
that the man you knew is gone.

1561
02:49:07.000 --> 02:49:10.583
I promised to love you until I died.
and for a long time after that.

1562
02:49:11.500 --> 02:49:12.833
And I will always love you.

1563
02:49:13.500 --> 02:49:15.875
But it is no longer in my power
to give you happiness.

1564
02:49:17.042 --> 02:49:19.042
All I can offer you now is consolation.

1565
02:49:20.500 --> 02:49:21.833
Your son will be happy.

1566
02:49:22.750 --> 02:49:26.000
Albert and Haydée
will live out the story we couldn't.

1567
02:49:26.542 --> 02:49:27.958
Happiness to our children.

1568
02:49:28.667 --> 02:49:31.583
who will outlive us
and taste the sweetness of love.

1569
02:49:33.417 --> 02:49:36.042
As I write to you.
I'm living out my last moments with you.

1570
02:49:36.750 --> 02:49:39.583
Everything after it will be memories.

1571
02:49:40.458 --> 02:49:42.583
I will take them with me to the sea.

1572
02:49:43.542 --> 02:49:46.208
The one place on earth
where everything is horizon

1573
02:49:46.292 --> 02:49:48.542
and there are no traces left by men.

1574
02:49:50.375 --> 02:49:52.375
Live and be happy.

1575
02:49:53.333 --> 02:49:57.542
Never forget. until the day
when fate can bring us together again.

1576
02:49:58.250 --> 02:50:01.167
that all human wisdom is in these two words.

1577
02:50:01.708 --> 02:50:03.875
"waiting" and "hoping."

1578
02:50:06.708 --> 02:50:10.250
Edmond Dantés. The Count of Monte Cristo.

1578
